1
00:02:02,916 --> 00:02:04,958
Don't wolf it down, Hiro.

2
00:02:05,750 --> 00:02:07,250
You'll choke!

3
00:02:08,875 --> 00:02:09,833
Let's go.

4
00:02:46,458 --> 00:02:50,916
<i>Statistically, 50.8% of Japanese over 60</i>

5
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:54,625
<i>remain in the workforce.</i>

6
00:02:54,708 --> 00:02:58,500
{\an8}So why do I have to retire?

7
00:02:59,083 --> 00:03:02,916
{\an8}<i>Hiro, we've extended</i>
<i>your contract many times.</i>

8
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:06,083
{\an8}<i>Please just accept</i>
<i>your retirement gracefully.</i>

9
00:03:06,166 --> 00:03:07,416
<i>Hiro,</i>

10
00:03:08,083 --> 00:03:09,625
<i>on behalf of the company,</i>

11
00:03:10,375 --> 00:03:12,250
<i>thank you</i>

12
00:03:12,333 --> 00:03:14,916
<i>for all your years of serv--</i>

13
00:03:22,166 --> 00:03:24,250
Hiro, please.

14
00:03:24,333 --> 00:03:27,541
I can't let you work here anymore.

15
00:03:27,625 --> 00:03:29,833
My neck was stiff for six months,

16
00:03:29,916 --> 00:03:32,041
and I still came back to work.

17
00:03:33,333 --> 00:03:37,458
Also, I've worked here

18
00:03:37,541 --> 00:03:39,708
my whole life.

19
00:03:39,791 --> 00:03:41,291
You gave me this award.

20
00:03:41,375 --> 00:03:44,458
-Doesn't it prick your conscience at all?
-Exactly.

21
00:03:44,541 --> 00:03:46,375
Look, look!

22
00:03:46,458 --> 00:03:48,083
I've worked on that model

23
00:03:48,166 --> 00:03:51,625
since the prototype.

24
00:03:52,791 --> 00:03:54,458
Prototype.

25
00:03:56,083 --> 00:03:59,750
Dream on if you think I'll retire,

26
00:03:59,833 --> 00:04:01,291
Tat.

27
00:04:02,375 --> 00:04:03,208
Here.

28
00:04:07,625 --> 00:04:09,708
Yikes. Rough day?

29
00:04:10,875 --> 00:04:11,875
Put them in here.

30
00:04:27,333 --> 00:04:29,458
Gosh.

31
00:04:44,958 --> 00:04:46,041
There we go.

32
00:04:49,708 --> 00:04:51,375
Gosh…

33
00:05:09,958 --> 00:05:10,791
All right.

34
00:05:38,500 --> 00:05:41,083
How did you end up in here?

35
00:05:43,416 --> 00:05:45,541
Nice to meet you.

36
00:05:48,708 --> 00:05:50,375
What's up?

37
00:05:51,416 --> 00:05:53,166
Are you hungry?

38
00:06:12,291 --> 00:06:14,666
Cheers!

39
00:06:49,583 --> 00:06:52,916
<i>So you're the new engineer?</i>

40
00:06:53,000 --> 00:06:54,458
<i>Here.</i>

41
00:06:54,541 --> 00:06:57,625
<i>Your employee card.</i>

42
00:06:57,708 --> 00:06:59,708
<i>Do your best.</i>

43
00:07:00,666 --> 00:07:03,708
<i>Listen, newbie.</i>

44
00:07:03,791 --> 00:07:08,458
<i>You must know every part inside out.</i>

45
00:07:08,541 --> 00:07:11,000
<i>Hiro.</i>

46
00:07:13,666 --> 00:07:15,500
Be quiet, okay?

47
00:07:15,583 --> 00:07:16,708
Understand?

48
00:07:17,833 --> 00:07:20,666
Hang in there.

49
00:07:24,541 --> 00:07:28,375
-Hello, Hiro!
-Morning.

50
00:07:28,458 --> 00:07:30,083
It's cold today.

51
00:07:35,250 --> 00:07:37,583
Going fishing after work?

52
00:07:37,666 --> 00:07:39,875
Take me with you.

53
00:08:12,958 --> 00:08:14,250
Little guy.

54
00:08:15,500 --> 00:08:16,583
Come on out.

55
00:08:19,375 --> 00:08:20,916
I can't look after you.

56
00:08:22,541 --> 00:08:24,541
Go on now.

57
00:08:25,625 --> 00:08:27,166
Stay here.

58
00:08:27,250 --> 00:08:29,583
Pets aren't allowed at my condo.

59
00:08:29,666 --> 00:08:31,416
Don't run into the street.

60
00:08:31,500 --> 00:08:32,583
It's dangerous.

61
00:08:33,416 --> 00:08:34,625
I have to go.

62
00:08:34,708 --> 00:08:35,666
Bye.

63
00:08:43,916 --> 00:08:45,125
Hey!

64
00:08:45,208 --> 00:08:47,583
Paitoon. Why did you get out of the car?

65
00:08:47,666 --> 00:08:49,583
We're already late. Let's go!

66
00:08:49,666 --> 00:08:52,875
Wait! HR sent me to pick up the new hire.

67
00:08:59,666 --> 00:09:01,166
Hello. You're Paitoon, right?

68
00:09:02,125 --> 00:09:03,875
His Thai is excellent!

69
00:09:03,958 --> 00:09:06,000
Hello, I'm Sawada.

70
00:09:06,083 --> 00:09:09,708
I've been appointed Chief Engineer.
Looking forward to learning from you.

71
00:09:10,375 --> 00:09:12,208
I'm the new Chief Engineer.

72
00:09:14,333 --> 00:09:17,750
I'm still the Chief Engineer!

73
00:09:17,833 --> 00:09:20,333
The only one in the company.

74
00:09:20,416 --> 00:09:21,833
I haven't retired!

75
00:09:21,916 --> 00:09:22,916
Let's go.

76
00:09:31,041 --> 00:09:34,083
New kid, this is the drum test rule.

77
00:09:34,166 --> 00:09:35,625
Keep your eyes sharp,

78
00:09:35,708 --> 00:09:37,250
ears open,

79
00:09:37,333 --> 00:09:39,291
and snout on the scent.

80
00:09:39,375 --> 00:09:41,375
Feel the vibration.

81
00:09:41,458 --> 00:09:44,958
Use all of your five senses.

82
00:09:47,250 --> 00:09:49,125
That's the pursuit of perfection.

83
00:09:57,708 --> 00:09:59,250
This one's good to go.

84
00:10:00,375 --> 00:10:02,500
Back to work, everyone.

85
00:10:02,583 --> 00:10:04,250
President!

86
00:10:10,416 --> 00:10:13,708
I lost a round of rock-paper-scissors
to Hiro.

87
00:10:13,791 --> 00:10:16,208
The winner gets to test the car first.

88
00:10:22,125 --> 00:10:23,333
As of today,

89
00:10:23,416 --> 00:10:26,125
you are an outsider.

90
00:10:26,208 --> 00:10:28,583
You'll need permission
to enter the premises

91
00:10:28,666 --> 00:10:30,000
from here on.

92
00:10:43,666 --> 00:10:44,958
Do you need a hand?

93
00:10:45,041 --> 00:10:46,000
No.

94
00:10:51,500 --> 00:10:54,208
Shall I call a tuk-tuk for you?

95
00:11:03,041 --> 00:11:04,291
Little guy.

96
00:11:06,833 --> 00:11:08,958
Want to go on a trip?

97
00:11:21,291 --> 00:11:24,958
The other day, I was checking blueprints,

98
00:11:25,041 --> 00:11:27,083
leading a team,

99
00:11:28,000 --> 00:11:32,083
going to lunch and meetings.

100
00:11:32,666 --> 00:11:34,666
Today, I'm suddenly an outsider.

101
00:11:34,750 --> 00:11:37,375
How absurd.

102
00:11:40,375 --> 00:11:42,958
I'm healthier than ever.

103
00:11:43,041 --> 00:11:45,625
Without my work, what do I have left?

104
00:11:52,791 --> 00:11:55,000
You're adorable.

105
00:11:59,208 --> 00:12:00,916
I got one!

106
00:12:01,000 --> 00:12:02,416
Little guy!

107
00:12:02,500 --> 00:12:03,916
Little guy.

108
00:12:04,000 --> 00:12:05,833
Don't be scared.

109
00:12:06,916 --> 00:12:08,208
Hang on.

110
00:12:20,500 --> 00:12:22,416
So cute!

111
00:12:23,708 --> 00:12:25,833
It tastes good, you know?

112
00:12:40,125 --> 00:12:41,541
You want some?

113
00:12:49,500 --> 00:12:52,541
Your fur is white,

114
00:12:52,625 --> 00:12:54,375
just like lice.

115
00:12:54,458 --> 00:12:56,458
Wait. No.

116
00:12:56,541 --> 00:12:58,416
White, lice, rice.

117
00:12:58,500 --> 00:12:59,583
Head lice.

118
00:12:59,666 --> 00:13:00,833
The color white.

119
00:13:00,916 --> 00:13:02,291
Eat rice.

120
00:13:04,208 --> 00:13:06,166
Your fur is white,

121
00:13:06,250 --> 00:13:08,291
just like rice!

122
00:13:08,375 --> 00:13:09,250
Right?

123
00:13:15,458 --> 00:13:17,083
I shall call you…

124
00:13:17,166 --> 00:13:18,416
Gohan.

125
00:13:19,000 --> 00:13:20,916
Sound good? Gohan.

126
00:13:21,000 --> 00:13:23,916
All right.

127
00:13:24,000 --> 00:13:25,541
Gohan.

128
00:13:48,500 --> 00:13:51,041
Hey! You scared me!

129
00:13:51,125 --> 00:13:53,666
<i>Happy New Year!</i>

130
00:13:53,750 --> 00:13:56,083
<i>It's Hana.</i>

131
00:13:56,166 --> 00:14:00,541
I can't believe how fast you've grown.

132
00:14:01,291 --> 00:14:02,125
<i>So…</i>

133
00:14:02,750 --> 00:14:03,750
<i>how's your contract?</i>

134
00:14:05,125 --> 00:14:06,500
<i>Did they extend it?</i>

135
00:14:08,541 --> 00:14:10,416
<i>I take your silence as a no then.</i>

136
00:14:11,291 --> 00:14:13,958
<i>Don't you want to move back here?</i>

137
00:14:14,041 --> 00:14:16,166
<i>We could live nearby.</i>
<i>I'll find a place for you.</i>

138
00:14:16,833 --> 00:14:20,500
<i>You can take care</i>
<i>of this little rice ball.</i>

139
00:14:21,708 --> 00:14:25,458
<i>Hana…</i>

140
00:14:30,166 --> 00:14:34,083
Let's celebrate
New Year's together, Gohan.

141
00:14:35,166 --> 00:14:36,875
Hurry up, will you?

142
00:14:36,958 --> 00:14:39,708
Oh, look. It's midnight.
Can't sell booze anymore.

143
00:14:39,791 --> 00:14:40,833
Happy New Year.

144
00:14:43,583 --> 00:14:46,583
-Happy New Year.
-Happy New Year.

145
00:15:16,041 --> 00:15:16,958
Gohan!

146
00:15:20,791 --> 00:15:21,791
Gohan!

147
00:15:22,708 --> 00:15:23,708
Gohan!

148
00:15:24,333 --> 00:15:25,791
Gohan!

149
00:15:34,750 --> 00:15:35,666
Gohan.

150
00:15:50,000 --> 00:15:50,958
It's not him.

151
00:15:51,875 --> 00:15:53,375
Gohan!

152
00:15:57,000 --> 00:15:58,000
Gohan!

153
00:15:59,250 --> 00:16:00,125
Gohan!

154
00:16:14,500 --> 00:16:15,375
Gohan!

155
00:16:16,125 --> 00:16:16,958
Gohan.

156
00:16:17,666 --> 00:16:19,625
Sorry.

157
00:16:19,708 --> 00:16:20,625
Come here.

158
00:16:20,708 --> 00:16:22,125
This way.

159
00:16:22,208 --> 00:16:24,500
Don't be afraid.

160
00:16:24,583 --> 00:16:25,583
Come here.

161
00:16:25,666 --> 00:16:27,500
You're okay now.

162
00:16:28,250 --> 00:16:30,208
Come. All right.

163
00:16:32,625 --> 00:16:34,625
I'm glad you're okay.

164
00:16:35,708 --> 00:16:37,291
I'm so glad.

165
00:16:37,375 --> 00:16:38,875
You're safe now. Don't worry.

166
00:17:00,875 --> 00:17:03,750
Just wait here, okay?

167
00:17:11,500 --> 00:17:12,625
Gohan.

168
00:17:15,250 --> 00:17:16,375
Hey.

169
00:17:16,458 --> 00:17:18,708
Goodness.

170
00:17:20,916 --> 00:17:22,291
Come here.

171
00:17:22,375 --> 00:17:24,666
You can't do that.

172
00:17:24,750 --> 00:17:25,916
Here, chew on this first.

173
00:17:27,083 --> 00:17:29,041
That's it. Good boy.

174
00:17:54,625 --> 00:17:57,166
That's too bad.

175
00:17:58,083 --> 00:18:01,291
You will get used to it.

176
00:18:03,666 --> 00:18:05,375
I sympathize with you.

177
00:18:05,458 --> 00:18:08,125
I thought I could hold it in at first too.

178
00:18:08,208 --> 00:18:10,708
I have a lot of adult diapers in stock.

179
00:18:10,791 --> 00:18:12,375
Do you want to try one?

180
00:18:12,458 --> 00:18:14,625
Slips on just like underwear.

181
00:18:14,708 --> 00:18:15,916
No, thank you.

182
00:18:30,041 --> 00:18:31,500
I mean, sounds good!

183
00:18:31,583 --> 00:18:34,416
Teach me how to use it sometime, okay?

184
00:18:36,125 --> 00:18:38,166
I have a pack right here.

185
00:18:38,250 --> 00:18:39,583
I'll bring it over.

186
00:18:39,666 --> 00:18:40,875
Just a second.

187
00:18:40,958 --> 00:18:42,958
You don't have to do that!

188
00:18:43,041 --> 00:18:46,250
Just throw it here.

189
00:18:52,375 --> 00:18:53,750
I'm ready.

190
00:19:07,833 --> 00:19:08,833
Wow!

191
00:19:08,916 --> 00:19:09,916
Nice catch!

192
00:19:14,625 --> 00:19:16,041
What was that noise?

193
00:19:19,791 --> 00:19:22,000
Gohan.

194
00:19:26,708 --> 00:19:28,625
Nice job.

195
00:19:38,708 --> 00:19:39,708
Wow!

196
00:19:39,791 --> 00:19:41,416
Hitching a ride to go fishing?

197
00:19:43,833 --> 00:19:44,666
What?

198
00:19:45,333 --> 00:19:48,041
If you get kicked out,
I won't drive you home.

199
00:19:48,125 --> 00:19:48,958
Jeez!

200
00:19:51,416 --> 00:19:53,083
-Can I get in?
-Hell yes!

201
00:19:53,166 --> 00:19:54,541
What are you waiting for?

202
00:20:02,333 --> 00:20:03,458
Son of a…

203
00:20:04,541 --> 00:20:05,750
Dog!

204
00:20:05,833 --> 00:20:07,458
Whose dog did you steal?

205
00:20:08,833 --> 00:20:11,166
So cute!

206
00:20:11,250 --> 00:20:12,541
Is that your dog, Hiro?

207
00:20:13,791 --> 00:20:15,416
Shiro.

208
00:20:16,333 --> 00:20:18,541
His name is Gohan.

209
00:20:18,625 --> 00:20:21,666
Do not call him willy-nilly, please.

210
00:20:21,750 --> 00:20:24,625
And he's not my dog.

211
00:20:24,708 --> 00:20:28,083
I'm only his temporary home.

212
00:20:29,666 --> 00:20:31,750
Gohan.

213
00:20:31,833 --> 00:20:32,750
Cute!

214
00:20:33,375 --> 00:20:34,708
Gohan.

215
00:20:36,375 --> 00:20:37,208
Gohan.

216
00:20:43,041 --> 00:20:43,916
There.

217
00:20:44,000 --> 00:20:46,833
-So cute.
-Gohan.

218
00:21:00,958 --> 00:21:02,041
Hey.

219
00:21:03,416 --> 00:21:04,583
Hiro!

220
00:21:04,666 --> 00:21:06,500
What crazy scheme are you up to now?

221
00:21:06,583 --> 00:21:09,500
Didn't I tell you?
You're not allowed in here.

222
00:21:09,583 --> 00:21:13,041
Tat, I've decided to go back to Japan.

223
00:21:13,125 --> 00:21:14,666
I'm willing to retire.

224
00:21:15,250 --> 00:21:16,958
Really?

225
00:21:17,958 --> 00:21:20,541
I'll look for a new job in Japan

226
00:21:20,625 --> 00:21:24,958
once I find a home for this puppy.

227
00:21:28,458 --> 00:21:30,083
Thai people are kind.

228
00:21:30,166 --> 00:21:34,125
I'm sure I can find a new owner for Gohan.

229
00:21:34,208 --> 00:21:36,333
Give me two weeks.

230
00:21:37,125 --> 00:21:39,125
Please.

231
00:21:39,208 --> 00:21:41,791
-Please!
-Please!

232
00:21:41,875 --> 00:21:43,250
What's wrong with you all?

233
00:21:43,333 --> 00:21:45,875
Everyone wants a dog now?

234
00:21:45,958 --> 00:21:46,791
Yes!

235
00:21:51,666 --> 00:21:53,416
Isn't he adorable, sir?

236
00:21:54,208 --> 00:21:56,291
Cute, right?

237
00:21:58,166 --> 00:22:00,208
I give you one week.

238
00:22:00,291 --> 00:22:01,541
-Really?
-One week.

239
00:22:01,625 --> 00:22:03,208
Thank you, Tat.

240
00:22:03,291 --> 00:22:05,666
-Thank you, Tat!
-Thank you, Tat!

241
00:22:11,291 --> 00:22:13,791
-So cute!
-Gohan.

242
00:22:23,041 --> 00:22:24,500
Excuse me.

243
00:22:24,583 --> 00:22:27,416
Is this the place for adoption interviews?

244
00:22:27,500 --> 00:22:28,666
Please. Sit down.

245
00:22:28,750 --> 00:22:32,500
I've dreamed of having a dog
ever since I was a child.

246
00:22:32,583 --> 00:22:36,083
There used to be a stray in the alley
where I lived.

247
00:22:36,166 --> 00:22:38,208
It was so cute and loyal.

248
00:22:38,291 --> 00:22:41,250
Will you be keeping Gohan inside
or outside the house?

249
00:22:41,333 --> 00:22:44,583
In the alley, like when I was a kid.

250
00:22:45,208 --> 00:22:47,125
Let me take that into consideration.

251
00:22:47,208 --> 00:22:48,583
Thank you.

252
00:22:48,666 --> 00:22:53,458
How's that any different
from staying at 7-Eleven?

253
00:22:53,541 --> 00:22:54,833
Poor little guy.

254
00:22:54,916 --> 00:22:56,750
GOHAN'S ADOPTION INTERVIEWEE FORM

255
00:22:58,958 --> 00:23:00,333
I want to keep him indoors.

256
00:23:00,416 --> 00:23:01,708
He's safer inside the house.

257
00:23:01,791 --> 00:23:03,750
I'll keep him safe in an enclosed space.

258
00:23:03,833 --> 00:23:06,291
Will anyone be at home during the day?

259
00:23:06,375 --> 00:23:07,291
No.

260
00:23:07,375 --> 00:23:08,416
I live alone.

261
00:23:08,500 --> 00:23:10,000
I'll hurry back to him once I clock out.

262
00:23:10,083 --> 00:23:12,125
Let me consider it.

263
00:23:12,208 --> 00:23:13,666
Thank you.

264
00:23:15,333 --> 00:23:19,125
Leaving the dog alone
in the house all day?

265
00:23:19,208 --> 00:23:20,666
Gohan would be miserable.

266
00:23:23,458 --> 00:23:26,458
A dog in my neighborhood
was just poisoned.

267
00:23:26,541 --> 00:23:28,791
I should probably get a new guard dog.

268
00:23:28,875 --> 00:23:31,750
Gohan probably loves dragging stuff.

269
00:23:33,041 --> 00:23:34,625
Who the hell let you in here?

270
00:23:35,541 --> 00:23:40,208
May I ask what makes you, Ms. Sarocha,
a good fit for Gohan?

271
00:23:40,291 --> 00:23:43,166
Dear Hiro,

272
00:23:43,250 --> 00:23:46,208
respectfully,

273
00:23:46,291 --> 00:23:49,833
I've always been a dog lover.

274
00:23:49,916 --> 00:23:53,458
My house is fully fenced,

275
00:23:53,541 --> 00:23:55,500
with a lawn in front.

276
00:23:55,583 --> 00:24:00,458
My garden is lush and naturally shaded…

277
00:24:02,875 --> 00:24:06,416
Goodness. He's so cute! I can't!

278
00:24:06,500 --> 00:24:10,416
I really want him!
I promise. If I get to take care of him…

279
00:24:10,500 --> 00:24:12,333
He moved!

280
00:24:12,416 --> 00:24:14,708
Hey there, sweetie!

281
00:24:14,791 --> 00:24:15,833
Hold still!

282
00:24:15,916 --> 00:24:17,083
Oh, my god! So cute!

283
00:24:17,166 --> 00:24:18,833
-Look here!
-Stop!

284
00:24:18,916 --> 00:24:21,000
-What?
-He's going blind.

285
00:24:21,083 --> 00:24:22,750
-Blind?
-Please leave.

286
00:24:22,833 --> 00:24:25,041
I'll get him some medicine.
My neighborhood vet is…

287
00:24:25,833 --> 00:24:26,750
No, no.

288
00:24:36,166 --> 00:24:38,500
Has anyone adopted him yet?

289
00:24:39,708 --> 00:24:43,083
We live in the same condo, Sawada.

290
00:24:43,166 --> 00:24:45,333
They don't allow pets there.

291
00:24:45,416 --> 00:24:47,833
I'm not the one adopting him.

292
00:24:47,916 --> 00:24:48,958
It's…

293
00:24:51,250 --> 00:24:52,583
my girlfriend.

294
00:25:04,541 --> 00:25:06,416
Since Mali died,

295
00:25:06,500 --> 00:25:08,833
I haven't been able to get another dog.

296
00:25:09,416 --> 00:25:12,083
It took me years to get over Mali.

297
00:25:13,208 --> 00:25:16,833
But when Sawada showed me
pictures of Gohan,

298
00:25:16,916 --> 00:25:19,125
I felt like…

299
00:25:20,041 --> 00:25:21,625
it was destiny.

300
00:25:24,791 --> 00:25:26,625
The nose, in particular.

301
00:25:28,541 --> 00:25:29,875
Apart from Mali,

302
00:25:30,500 --> 00:25:33,208
I've never seen a dog with this nose.

303
00:25:36,875 --> 00:25:39,166
So Sawada and Meow,

304
00:25:39,250 --> 00:25:40,416
how did you two meet?

305
00:25:42,291 --> 00:25:44,583
-When Meow studied in Japan…
-When I studied in Japan…

306
00:25:46,125 --> 00:25:49,291
After I graduated,

307
00:25:49,375 --> 00:25:51,208
I came back to Si Racha.

308
00:25:51,291 --> 00:25:54,500
For this relationship to work,
Sawada had no choice.

309
00:25:54,583 --> 00:25:57,625
So I asked him to find work in Thailand.

310
00:26:00,041 --> 00:26:01,625
Gohan!

311
00:26:02,583 --> 00:26:05,291
Are you a dogzilla?
Quit raiding people's stuff!

312
00:26:05,375 --> 00:26:07,083
Get him out of there!

313
00:26:07,166 --> 00:26:09,583
He's so naughty. I'm sorry.

314
00:26:09,666 --> 00:26:11,208
It's fine.

315
00:26:11,291 --> 00:26:13,958
A naughty pup is a real pup.

316
00:26:18,750 --> 00:26:20,666
She's the patron saint of puppies.

317
00:26:23,250 --> 00:26:26,708
Good boy!

318
00:26:26,791 --> 00:26:28,666
You got it, Gohan.

319
00:26:28,750 --> 00:26:30,500
Give him a treat right away,

320
00:26:30,583 --> 00:26:32,208
so he'll get used to it.

321
00:26:36,125 --> 00:26:37,833
That's incredible.

322
00:26:37,916 --> 00:26:39,958
She nailed it on the first try.

323
00:26:40,041 --> 00:26:41,250
Here you go.

324
00:26:42,666 --> 00:26:46,125
Are you planning to have kids?

325
00:26:46,208 --> 00:26:48,458
We've already decided not to.

326
00:26:48,541 --> 00:26:50,125
-Right?
-Yes.

327
00:26:50,208 --> 00:26:51,250
Then…

328
00:26:51,333 --> 00:26:54,833
what if you two…

329
00:26:54,916 --> 00:26:55,875
break up?

330
00:26:58,375 --> 00:27:00,000
Who will take care of Gohan?

331
00:27:00,666 --> 00:27:02,250
Hey, that question's too personal.

332
00:27:03,000 --> 00:27:04,083
It's okay.

333
00:27:05,833 --> 00:27:07,791
In that case,

334
00:27:08,750 --> 00:27:10,875
I will take care of Gohan.

335
00:27:12,250 --> 00:27:16,125
If I decide to take care of him,

336
00:27:16,208 --> 00:27:17,958
it's for life.

337
00:27:19,041 --> 00:27:21,666
I wouldn't give Gohan to anyone else.

338
00:27:27,125 --> 00:27:28,291
Hiro.

339
00:27:28,375 --> 00:27:31,625
If you let Meow adopt Gohan,

340
00:27:31,708 --> 00:27:34,000
I'll come in second around here.

341
00:27:34,083 --> 00:27:36,458
But that's fine with me.

342
00:27:40,125 --> 00:27:42,291
Last question.

343
00:27:42,375 --> 00:27:45,541
What will Gohan's new name be?

344
00:27:49,875 --> 00:27:52,416
Gohan is already a perfect name.

345
00:28:04,458 --> 00:28:06,916
If you said Mali,

346
00:28:07,666 --> 00:28:09,583
I would've changed my mind.

347
00:28:29,208 --> 00:28:30,791
Wait…

348
00:28:30,875 --> 00:28:33,916
Let me consider it.

349
00:28:35,666 --> 00:28:36,500
What?

350
00:28:37,500 --> 00:28:38,666
Paitoon, let's go.

351
00:28:49,958 --> 00:28:51,125
Go ahead.

352
00:28:59,208 --> 00:29:02,083
It's obvious that you want to keep him.

353
00:29:02,166 --> 00:29:04,541
I can only look after him temporarily.

354
00:29:04,625 --> 00:29:07,458
I'm going back to Japan for work.

355
00:29:08,250 --> 00:29:11,458
You're still thinking of work at this age?

356
00:29:11,541 --> 00:29:13,958
Who cares about all this work nonsense?

357
00:29:14,041 --> 00:29:16,791
I don't like

358
00:29:16,875 --> 00:29:19,583
the phrase "who cares."

359
00:29:19,666 --> 00:29:22,416
Sounds irresponsible.

360
00:29:22,500 --> 00:29:25,541
What do you have to be responsible for?

361
00:29:25,625 --> 00:29:27,833
Your wife is long gone.

362
00:29:27,916 --> 00:29:31,375
Your son's grown up
and has his own family.

363
00:29:31,458 --> 00:29:34,083
If I were retired like you,

364
00:29:34,166 --> 00:29:37,958
I'd do nothing all day
except walk the dog.

365
00:29:38,041 --> 00:29:39,041
Life's good!

366
00:29:39,666 --> 00:29:43,208
I don't want to do nothing all day.

367
00:29:43,291 --> 00:29:47,958
So why didn't you give them the dog?
What are you waiting for?

368
00:29:48,041 --> 00:29:52,625
I have to consider it, just to be sure.

369
00:29:53,458 --> 00:29:55,333
Consider, my ass!

370
00:29:55,416 --> 00:29:58,958
I've known all along
that you want to keep him.

371
00:30:00,875 --> 00:30:01,833
I got one!

372
00:30:01,916 --> 00:30:03,083
Gohan!

373
00:30:03,166 --> 00:30:05,625
What kind of fish do you want today?

374
00:30:05,708 --> 00:30:06,708
Gohan.

375
00:30:09,125 --> 00:30:11,750
Where did Gohan go, Paitoon?

376
00:30:11,833 --> 00:30:13,000
I don't know.

377
00:30:13,583 --> 00:30:15,000
-Gohan!
-Gohan!

378
00:30:15,083 --> 00:30:16,708
Hold this!

379
00:30:16,791 --> 00:30:19,083
-You don't care about the fish anymore?
-Gohan!

380
00:30:19,166 --> 00:30:20,666
-Gohan!
-Gohan!

381
00:30:20,750 --> 00:30:22,375
Gohan!

382
00:30:23,083 --> 00:30:25,000
-Gohan!
-Gohan!

383
00:30:25,083 --> 00:30:26,333
Gohan!

384
00:30:26,416 --> 00:30:27,250
Gohan!

385
00:30:28,083 --> 00:30:29,458
Gohan!

386
00:30:29,541 --> 00:30:30,750
Gohan!

387
00:30:31,875 --> 00:30:32,916
Gohan!

388
00:30:35,125 --> 00:30:36,000
Gohan!

389
00:30:37,166 --> 00:30:38,208
Gohan!

390
00:30:38,291 --> 00:30:39,166
Gohan!

391
00:30:45,541 --> 00:30:46,916
Hiro!

392
00:30:47,000 --> 00:30:47,916
Don't jump…

393
00:30:50,833 --> 00:30:51,791
Too late.

394
00:30:53,958 --> 00:30:55,708
Hiro!

395
00:30:55,791 --> 00:30:56,875
Oh, man!

396
00:30:57,500 --> 00:30:58,875
Hold on!

397
00:31:00,041 --> 00:31:00,958
Hiro!

398
00:31:01,041 --> 00:31:02,625
Gohan is here!

399
00:31:03,541 --> 00:31:04,833
He's here!

400
00:31:05,875 --> 00:31:07,625
What a relief!

401
00:31:07,708 --> 00:31:09,583
He's here!

402
00:31:09,666 --> 00:31:11,583
I have him!

403
00:31:29,333 --> 00:31:30,375
Gohan.

404
00:31:31,166 --> 00:31:32,083
Want to pee?

405
00:31:32,166 --> 00:31:34,083
Do it here. Over here.

406
00:31:35,333 --> 00:31:37,791
Here…

407
00:31:38,875 --> 00:31:40,750
Over here!

408
00:32:07,875 --> 00:32:09,000
Paitoon.

409
00:32:09,083 --> 00:32:10,666
Drive slowly.

410
00:32:26,166 --> 00:32:27,166
Good morning.

411
00:32:29,916 --> 00:32:31,166
I've…

412
00:32:31,250 --> 00:32:33,958
considered it.

413
00:32:34,041 --> 00:32:37,708
Meow is going to take better care
of Gohan than I do.

414
00:32:46,166 --> 00:32:48,666
Open it after I leave, please.

415
00:33:19,291 --> 00:33:20,958
Thank you.

416
00:33:25,958 --> 00:33:27,500
BEST EMPLOYER AND SERVICE AWARD 2010

417
00:34:02,083 --> 00:34:04,166
To our company's living legend,

418
00:34:04,250 --> 00:34:08,041
return home with happiness, Hiro.

419
00:34:08,791 --> 00:34:09,750
Thank you.

420
00:34:11,000 --> 00:34:12,416
Sawada,

421
00:34:12,500 --> 00:34:14,750
I'll leave it to you.

422
00:34:17,208 --> 00:34:18,208
The pursuit of perfection.

423
00:34:21,750 --> 00:34:25,708
<i>Don't make me fall in love</i>

424
00:34:25,791 --> 00:34:29,791
<i>I'll get smitten, I'll fall too fast</i>

425
00:34:29,875 --> 00:34:34,458
<i>Love's stuck deep in my heart</i>
<i>What can I do?</i>

426
00:34:34,541 --> 00:34:37,208
<i>Try to pull it out, I just can't</i>

427
00:34:37,291 --> 00:34:41,625
<i>Don't make me think you feel it</i>
<i>If you don't</i>

428
00:34:41,708 --> 00:34:45,541
<i>If I get it wrong, I won't take the blame</i>

429
00:34:45,625 --> 00:34:51,166
<i>If I hug you, what would you say?</i>

430
00:35:28,625 --> 00:35:30,416
Straight to the airport?

431
00:35:37,250 --> 00:35:39,666
Hey, man.

432
00:35:42,750 --> 00:35:44,083
You'll trip!

433
00:35:45,708 --> 00:35:47,041
Paitoon, wait here.

434
00:35:47,125 --> 00:35:48,541
I'll be quick.

435
00:35:54,375 --> 00:35:55,958
Oh, for crying out loud.

436
00:35:56,041 --> 00:35:57,875
The doorbell is right there.

437
00:35:57,958 --> 00:35:59,291
Look at us, seriously.

438
00:35:59,375 --> 00:36:00,375
No need.

439
00:36:03,125 --> 00:36:04,875
That's enough already.

440
00:36:05,666 --> 00:36:07,208
You're going to miss your flight.

441
00:36:07,291 --> 00:36:08,625
Wait.

442
00:36:11,750 --> 00:36:13,458
What's wrong?

443
00:36:13,541 --> 00:36:14,416
What happened?

444
00:36:14,500 --> 00:36:16,708
What is it?

445
00:36:18,375 --> 00:36:21,041
Gohan, we'll dig later.
Let's go for a walk.

446
00:36:21,125 --> 00:36:22,541
Come quick.

447
00:36:22,625 --> 00:36:24,750
Gohan.

448
00:36:24,833 --> 00:36:26,541
Good boy! Come here!

449
00:36:26,625 --> 00:36:28,666
Let's go for a walk. Come.

450
00:36:28,750 --> 00:36:30,125
No! Don't go that way.

451
00:36:30,208 --> 00:36:31,375
This way.

452
00:36:31,458 --> 00:36:32,833
Come this way.

453
00:36:33,625 --> 00:36:36,250
Quick. Gohan!

454
00:36:36,333 --> 00:36:39,750
Good boy. Let's go.

455
00:36:42,875 --> 00:36:44,375
-Paitoon, let's go.
-Okay.

456
00:36:56,458 --> 00:36:57,500
Gohan!

457
00:36:59,166 --> 00:37:00,041
Gohan!

458
00:37:05,791 --> 00:37:06,625
Gohan!

459
00:37:09,500 --> 00:37:10,666
Paitoon!

460
00:37:10,750 --> 00:37:11,833
-What?
-Stop the car!

461
00:37:11,916 --> 00:37:12,958
What?

462
00:37:13,041 --> 00:37:15,708
-Stop the car!
-Gohan!

463
00:37:30,500 --> 00:37:31,791
Gohan.

464
00:37:31,875 --> 00:37:34,708
How did you know it was me?

465
00:37:39,041 --> 00:37:40,958
Was it the sound of the car?

466
00:37:42,500 --> 00:37:43,833
It was, wasn't it?

467
00:37:44,625 --> 00:37:47,166
You heard this car
every morning, didn't you?

468
00:37:49,416 --> 00:37:50,416
Meow.

469
00:37:51,000 --> 00:37:52,916
Please forgive me.

470
00:37:53,875 --> 00:37:57,125
I'm not here to take Gohan back.

471
00:37:58,166 --> 00:38:00,875
I'll get going now.

472
00:38:01,541 --> 00:38:04,500
Do you know that this past week,

473
00:38:05,458 --> 00:38:08,375
whenever a car drove by our house,

474
00:38:08,458 --> 00:38:10,416
Gohan would run to the window?

475
00:38:11,208 --> 00:38:12,458
Really?

476
00:38:12,541 --> 00:38:15,208
He waits for you every day.

477
00:38:20,583 --> 00:38:21,791
It's destiny.

478
00:38:25,000 --> 00:38:26,875
Gohan chose you.

479
00:38:33,916 --> 00:38:35,958
What about your "work in Japan"?

480
00:38:38,166 --> 00:38:40,083
Who cares, Paitoon?

481
00:38:43,166 --> 00:38:44,416
Who cares!

482
00:38:53,291 --> 00:38:54,916
Snoopy and Charlie.

483
00:39:04,166 --> 00:39:05,791
There you go.

484
00:39:05,875 --> 00:39:08,458
Looking sharp!

485
00:39:15,416 --> 00:39:17,833
<i>Hello, Dad.</i>

486
00:39:17,916 --> 00:39:19,958
<i>How's your new house?</i>

487
00:39:20,041 --> 00:39:22,291
Gohan, wait up!

488
00:39:22,375 --> 00:39:26,583
<i>I like it. No more elevators.</i>

489
00:39:26,666 --> 00:39:27,583
<i>I see.</i>

490
00:39:28,333 --> 00:39:30,500
<i>And how's your new job going?</i>

491
00:39:31,416 --> 00:39:32,916
<i>Well…</i>

492
00:39:33,000 --> 00:39:35,625
<i>It's pretty challenging.</i>

493
00:39:48,250 --> 00:39:52,750
<i>There's still a lot for me to learn.</i>

494
00:41:21,125 --> 00:41:22,500
All right!

495
00:41:26,041 --> 00:41:27,625
Today was fun, huh?

496
00:41:29,625 --> 00:41:31,291
Time for bed.

497
00:41:38,375 --> 00:41:40,791
Good night, Gohan.

498
00:43:03,500 --> 00:43:04,791
Are you hungry?

499
00:43:11,250 --> 00:43:12,083
Here.

500
00:43:45,625 --> 00:43:47,125
Help me carry him.

501
00:44:02,791 --> 00:44:05,000
Easy, buddy. It's okay.

502
00:44:16,000 --> 00:44:16,958
Here.

503
00:44:17,041 --> 00:44:18,083
Dog sedative.

504
00:44:18,166 --> 00:44:19,583
To calm him down.

505
00:44:19,666 --> 00:44:20,791
Quickly.

506
00:44:21,458 --> 00:44:22,750
Do you understand Thai?

507
00:44:23,500 --> 00:44:24,416
Yes.

508
00:44:24,500 --> 00:44:25,916
One shot and it'll be over.

509
00:44:26,583 --> 00:44:28,083
Push the plunger all the way.

510
00:44:49,333 --> 00:44:51,458
KUNG'S DOG SHELTER,
DONATE TO SAVE A STRAY'S LIFE

511
00:44:52,750 --> 00:44:54,916
<i>Hello, it's Kung here,</i>

512
00:44:55,000 --> 00:44:57,375
<i>giving you an update on Gohan.</i>

513
00:44:57,458 --> 00:45:00,791
<i>As you know, Gohan's Japanese owner</i>

514
00:45:00,875 --> 00:45:03,458
<i>passed away from COVID last week.</i>

515
00:45:03,541 --> 00:45:06,750
{\an8}<i>The rescue team was notified</i>
<i>of a COVID-related death.</i>

516
00:45:06,833 --> 00:45:09,083
{\an8}<i>The deceased was</i>
<i>a 70-year-old Japanese man.</i>

517
00:45:09,166 --> 00:45:15,333
{\an8}<i>His faithful dog, Gohan,</i>
<i>stayed by his side.</i>

518
00:45:15,416 --> 00:45:16,250
{\an8}<i>Think about it.</i>

519
00:45:16,875 --> 00:45:19,541
{\an8}<i>If a person gets COVID,</i>
<i>they will receive help.</i>

520
00:45:19,625 --> 00:45:21,166
{\an8}DOG GUARDS OWNER
WHO PASSED AWAY FROM COVID

521
00:45:21,250 --> 00:45:22,958
{\an8}<i>But no one dares to help the dog.</i>

522
00:45:23,041 --> 00:45:24,916
{\an8}<i>They don't want to risk getting exposed.</i>

523
00:45:25,000 --> 00:45:27,833
{\an8}<i>The rescue team contacted my shelter.</i>

524
00:45:29,583 --> 00:45:30,541
{\an8}<i>When I found Gohan,</i>

525
00:45:30,625 --> 00:45:34,375
he was lying very still in the dark.

526
00:45:34,458 --> 00:45:36,375
I could tell that he was hungry

527
00:45:36,458 --> 00:45:37,500
and sick.

528
00:45:37,583 --> 00:45:39,500
His eyes were…

529
00:45:40,458 --> 00:45:42,250
He looked so depressed,

530
00:45:42,333 --> 00:45:45,583
as if waiting for his owner to return.

531
00:45:46,750 --> 00:45:48,958
But his owner is already gone.

532
00:45:55,375 --> 00:45:59,541
<i>Gohan, time to eat!</i>

533
00:46:15,500 --> 00:46:16,541
Gohan.

534
00:46:17,916 --> 00:46:19,166
Welcome to your new home.

535
00:46:20,875 --> 00:46:23,166
Moe Thee, her salary is five grand.

536
00:46:23,250 --> 00:46:25,250
Her arms are smaller than a dog's legs.

537
00:46:25,333 --> 00:46:27,000
She's got no paperwork too.

538
00:46:27,791 --> 00:46:29,333
Can you talk to her?

539
00:46:29,916 --> 00:46:30,750
Here.

540
00:46:33,000 --> 00:46:34,291
Yes?

541
00:46:34,375 --> 00:46:36,041
<i>Five grand is not bad.</i>

542
00:46:36,125 --> 00:46:38,333
<i>It's better than struggling in Myanmar.</i>

543
00:46:38,416 --> 00:46:41,083
<i>Work for five to six months.</i>

544
00:46:41,166 --> 00:46:43,791
<i>Save up for your permit,</i>
<i>then find other work.</i>

545
00:46:43,875 --> 00:46:45,333
<i>Okay?</i>

546
00:46:45,416 --> 00:46:47,208
All right.

547
00:46:48,541 --> 00:46:49,583
Okay then.

548
00:46:51,750 --> 00:46:52,750
Wait.

549
00:46:53,791 --> 00:46:55,958
There's one rule here.

550
00:46:57,750 --> 00:46:58,958
No phones allowed.

551
00:47:04,666 --> 00:47:06,791
Or should I call Moe Thee
to come pick you up?

552
00:47:08,208 --> 00:47:10,208
Okay, sir.

553
00:47:14,666 --> 00:47:18,375
Just use my phone
if there's anything urgent.

554
00:47:21,291 --> 00:47:25,291
KUNG'S DOG SHELTER

555
00:47:36,750 --> 00:47:37,708
Keep it.

556
00:47:38,291 --> 00:47:39,291
Go in.

557
00:47:55,750 --> 00:47:58,041
Your Burmese name is hard to pronounce.

558
00:47:58,125 --> 00:47:59,875
Let's just call you Namcha.

559
00:48:02,500 --> 00:48:03,791
Your job is

560
00:48:03,875 --> 00:48:05,541
to feed the dogs food and water.

561
00:48:06,375 --> 00:48:08,083
Take them out to do their business.

562
00:48:09,041 --> 00:48:11,416
All 30 of them here.

563
00:48:12,333 --> 00:48:13,500
Got it?

564
00:48:20,208 --> 00:48:22,458
Feed them every other day.

565
00:48:22,541 --> 00:48:23,750
We're in a pandemic.

566
00:48:23,833 --> 00:48:25,958
Donations are thin.

567
00:48:28,250 --> 00:48:29,833
Hold on.

568
00:48:30,791 --> 00:48:32,500
Shit. All the cages are full.

569
00:48:45,416 --> 00:48:46,458
Dum!

570
00:48:46,541 --> 00:48:47,875
Easy there.

571
00:48:54,958 --> 00:48:57,125
-Put him in there.
-Okay.

572
00:49:17,125 --> 00:49:18,416
Sit down.

573
00:49:18,500 --> 00:49:20,791
Come on.

574
00:50:16,250 --> 00:50:20,625
Hi, guys. I have an update on Gohan.

575
00:50:20,708 --> 00:50:24,583
He's still pretty weak right now

576
00:50:24,666 --> 00:50:27,333
due to blood parasites.

577
00:50:30,000 --> 00:50:34,208
If you would like to sponsor
Gohan's treatment,

578
00:50:34,291 --> 00:50:37,666
please transfer the funds
to the shelter's account.

579
00:50:37,750 --> 00:50:38,750
I'LL DONATE TO GOHAN EVERY MONTH.

580
00:50:38,833 --> 00:50:40,458
MY DONATION TO GOHAN.

581
00:50:40,541 --> 00:50:42,083
RECOVER SOON, GOHAN.

582
00:50:42,166 --> 00:50:43,750
GET WELL SOON, GOHAN.

583
00:50:43,833 --> 00:50:44,875
ROOTING FOR YOU, GOHAN.

584
00:50:52,708 --> 00:50:54,333
<i>I promise I'll do my best</i>

585
00:50:54,416 --> 00:50:56,916
<i>to take care of Gohan.</i>

586
00:51:06,000 --> 00:51:07,791
I'm sorry.

587
00:51:09,583 --> 00:51:12,333
If I'd known,
I wouldn't have helped capture you.

588
00:51:13,458 --> 00:51:16,708
I'll be here by your side.

589
00:51:25,083 --> 00:51:26,291
Time for bed.

590
00:51:33,416 --> 00:51:35,791
Not for long now.

591
00:52:09,875 --> 00:52:12,250
Quickly.

592
00:52:28,166 --> 00:52:29,708
I've got enough savings,

593
00:52:29,791 --> 00:52:31,291
so I'm leaving now.

594
00:52:33,708 --> 00:52:35,916
This is all I can do for you guys.

595
00:52:36,625 --> 00:52:40,958
Go as far as you can. Understand?

596
00:52:41,041 --> 00:52:43,458
Stay and you'll end up like Dum.

597
00:53:32,875 --> 00:53:34,000
This one.

598
00:53:34,875 --> 00:53:36,458
MOBILE SHOP

599
00:53:36,541 --> 00:53:38,791
It's fully charged, ready to use.

600
00:53:42,583 --> 00:53:44,208
Let me check if the camera works.

601
00:53:45,500 --> 00:53:46,958
Smile!

602
00:53:59,708 --> 00:54:00,708
Gohan!

603
00:54:01,375 --> 00:54:03,125
Why are you following me?

604
00:54:03,208 --> 00:54:05,000
Go on!

605
00:54:06,000 --> 00:54:07,166
Get out of here!

606
00:54:10,375 --> 00:54:12,916
I'm going to look
for a new job in Bangkok.

607
00:54:13,708 --> 00:54:15,083
I can't even manage myself.

608
00:54:15,166 --> 00:54:17,208
How can I look after you?

609
00:54:20,541 --> 00:54:22,708
Go look for your new home! Go on!

610
00:54:23,333 --> 00:54:24,166
Go.

611
00:54:32,875 --> 00:54:34,958
You're going to get me in trouble.

612
00:54:53,125 --> 00:54:54,250
Hey.

613
00:54:54,333 --> 00:54:57,750
If you want to come along,
stay still and be quiet.

614
00:55:02,666 --> 00:55:04,375
<i>Passengers going to Bangkok,</i>

615
00:55:04,458 --> 00:55:07,333
<i>please board the bus at Platform One.</i>

616
00:55:33,583 --> 00:55:38,791
{\an8}TO MOE THEE: TRANSFERRED.
COMING FOR MY PERMIT.

617
00:55:50,291 --> 00:55:51,958
I'm on my way.

618
00:55:52,833 --> 00:55:54,958
Yes, it's the same price we agreed on.

619
00:55:55,791 --> 00:55:57,833
He's sitting right beside me.

620
00:56:00,500 --> 00:56:02,250
I know the driver.

621
00:56:03,000 --> 00:56:04,625
He made an exception.

622
00:56:07,250 --> 00:56:09,583
We'll be arriving soon.

623
00:56:13,916 --> 00:56:16,708
They're going to mate him with their hen.

624
00:56:16,791 --> 00:56:18,500
Yes, around a hundred thousand.

625
00:56:18,583 --> 00:56:21,166
Well, he's been through countless fights.

626
00:56:24,166 --> 00:56:27,916
Don't be sad. Come on in first.
We can talk about it later.

627
00:56:38,791 --> 00:56:40,666
Hell no!

628
00:56:41,875 --> 00:56:43,583
Why is there a dog on the bus?

629
00:56:45,125 --> 00:56:47,125
Help!

630
00:56:59,291 --> 00:57:00,125
Gohan!

631
00:57:01,166 --> 00:57:03,333
How are we going to make it to Bangkok?

632
00:57:04,666 --> 00:57:06,916
I can't afford to hire a car.

633
00:57:09,041 --> 00:57:10,125
You're unbelievable.

634
00:57:11,458 --> 00:57:13,000
Just get lost.

635
00:57:13,083 --> 00:57:14,166
Go.

636
00:57:15,875 --> 00:57:18,708
Are you arguing with me?

637
00:57:18,791 --> 00:57:20,166
Don't you dare.

638
00:57:23,666 --> 00:57:24,791
Shall I dump you here?

639
00:57:35,291 --> 00:57:36,875
Come here.

640
00:57:38,333 --> 00:57:39,958
Sit down.

641
00:57:44,750 --> 00:57:47,625
I could eat you up, you rascal!

642
00:57:59,875 --> 00:58:01,333
Go that way.

643
00:58:10,666 --> 00:58:13,416
Gohan, quickly!

644
00:58:41,625 --> 00:58:42,458
Gohan?

645
00:58:54,958 --> 00:58:56,875
That's clever.

646
00:58:56,958 --> 00:59:00,750
Let's turn you into a golden retriever.

647
00:59:17,000 --> 00:59:18,125
All done.

648
00:59:18,208 --> 00:59:19,708
Ready to go?

649
00:59:21,083 --> 00:59:22,625
Okay. Good boy!

650
00:59:22,708 --> 00:59:24,083
Let's go.

651
00:59:27,375 --> 00:59:28,375
GOHAN

652
00:59:28,458 --> 00:59:29,500
This dog?

653
00:59:30,291 --> 00:59:32,708
Yes, this white one!

654
00:59:32,791 --> 00:59:34,416
She snuck it onto the bus.

655
00:59:34,500 --> 00:59:36,791
I kicked them out along the way.

656
00:59:36,875 --> 00:59:38,416
-Are you sure?
-Yes!

657
00:59:38,500 --> 00:59:39,625
Damn it!

658
00:59:59,208 --> 01:00:02,250
Moe Thee,
your worker is causing trouble again.

659
01:00:04,125 --> 01:00:05,375
<i>What did she do?</i>

660
01:00:05,458 --> 01:00:06,958
<i>She took my fucking dog!</i>

661
01:00:23,291 --> 01:00:27,375
MOE THEE, 15 MISSED CALLS

662
01:00:29,916 --> 01:00:32,833
<i>What have you done?</i>

663
01:00:32,916 --> 01:00:35,333
<i>Kung is about to rip my head off!</i>

664
01:00:35,416 --> 01:00:36,958
<i>If I don't bring you back,</i>

665
01:00:37,041 --> 01:00:39,208
<i>he'll report me for smuggling workers.</i>

666
01:00:39,291 --> 01:00:40,750
He wouldn't dare call the cops.

667
01:00:41,541 --> 01:00:43,208
<i>What do you mean?</i>

668
01:00:48,625 --> 01:00:51,791
Do you know what kind of person he is?

669
01:00:54,208 --> 01:00:59,333
How he abuses all the dogs?

670
01:01:00,666 --> 01:01:02,833
<i>So you stole one and ran away with it?</i>

671
01:01:03,583 --> 01:01:05,250
I didn't steal!

672
01:01:06,625 --> 01:01:08,125
He followed me.

673
01:01:09,125 --> 01:01:12,125
<i>You want to go to jail over a damn dog?</i>

674
01:01:12,208 --> 01:01:14,916
<i>I'm in deep shit because of you!</i>

675
01:01:15,625 --> 01:01:18,666
Just give me my permit
if you don't want trouble.

676
01:01:21,083 --> 01:01:24,583
<i>Fine. I'll send you the location</i>
<i>for tomorrow.</i>

677
01:01:24,666 --> 01:01:28,250
<i>You'll get your permit</i>
<i>and we're done here.</i>

678
01:01:42,166 --> 01:01:43,583
Gohan.

679
01:01:44,333 --> 01:01:46,291
Why are you licking the fridge?

680
01:01:53,083 --> 01:01:55,250
You really want those brownies?

681
01:01:56,875 --> 01:01:59,875
Dogs can't have chocolate.

682
01:02:01,875 --> 01:02:03,875
If you want it that badly,

683
01:02:03,958 --> 01:02:05,833
should I just call you Brownie?

684
01:02:07,375 --> 01:02:08,291
Oh?

685
01:02:10,083 --> 01:02:11,416
You like this name?

686
01:02:12,708 --> 01:02:14,916
Let's see.

687
01:02:16,041 --> 01:02:16,875
Strawberry?

688
01:02:20,791 --> 01:02:21,916
Cookie?

689
01:02:23,041 --> 01:02:24,000
Muffin?

690
01:02:25,666 --> 01:02:26,583
Brownie?

691
01:02:32,958 --> 01:02:35,250
Okay.

692
01:02:35,333 --> 01:02:37,708
From now on,

693
01:02:38,375 --> 01:02:42,541
you'd better respond to "Brownie."

694
01:02:44,708 --> 01:02:45,750
Brownie.

695
01:02:47,916 --> 01:02:49,625
Such a good boy!

696
01:03:08,541 --> 01:03:10,041
Back home in Myanmar,

697
01:03:10,833 --> 01:03:12,500
there was a stray dog.

698
01:03:15,333 --> 01:03:17,083
My family wouldn't let me keep it,

699
01:03:18,458 --> 01:03:22,625
but I snuck out to play with it every day.

700
01:03:25,125 --> 01:03:26,708
My mom told me

701
01:03:28,083 --> 01:03:30,583
not to name it

702
01:03:31,416 --> 01:03:34,291
or I'd start getting attached.

703
01:03:37,750 --> 01:03:40,750
You're the first dog I'd ever named.

704
01:03:40,833 --> 01:03:44,333
BROWNIE

705
01:03:44,416 --> 01:03:46,375
Good night,

706
01:03:47,125 --> 01:03:48,125
Brownie.

707
01:03:53,875 --> 01:03:54,791
Brownie?

708
01:03:58,583 --> 01:03:59,500
Brownie?

709
01:04:07,708 --> 01:04:08,625
Brownie!

710
01:04:09,750 --> 01:04:10,791
It sniffed around,

711
01:04:10,875 --> 01:04:12,916
then jumped in and got comfy.

712
01:04:13,000 --> 01:04:14,833
I'm really sorry!

713
01:04:15,458 --> 01:04:17,166
Brownie, what are you doing here?

714
01:04:17,250 --> 01:04:18,666
You're bothering his fish!

715
01:04:18,750 --> 01:04:20,166
Where are you from?

716
01:04:21,791 --> 01:04:23,458
I'm from Myawaddy.

717
01:04:24,083 --> 01:04:25,333
I'm from Bago.

718
01:04:26,166 --> 01:04:28,333
So where are you headed?

719
01:04:33,625 --> 01:04:35,125
Want a ride with Jumbo to Bangkok?

720
01:04:38,416 --> 01:04:40,833
Shall we go with them, Brownie?

721
01:05:04,291 --> 01:05:08,208
MEET HERE AT 8 P.M.

722
01:05:10,166 --> 01:05:11,541
-Thank you.
-Sure.

723
01:05:11,625 --> 01:05:12,666
Let's go!

724
01:05:16,041 --> 01:05:17,833
Come on.

725
01:05:29,333 --> 01:05:31,083
No. Come here.

726
01:05:52,083 --> 01:05:56,041
Look over there.

727
01:05:56,125 --> 01:05:59,333
We'll come back to play next time, okay?

728
01:05:59,416 --> 01:06:00,958
We have to go now.

729
01:06:03,708 --> 01:06:04,625
Hi, there.

730
01:06:06,708 --> 01:06:10,416
When Moe Thee heard "immigration,"
he spilled.

731
01:06:10,500 --> 01:06:11,750
-Please!
-Come quickly!

732
01:06:11,833 --> 01:06:14,208
Please let the dog go!

733
01:06:14,291 --> 01:06:15,708
I can work for free!

734
01:06:15,791 --> 01:06:17,416
Let the dog go? Are you insane?

735
01:06:18,041 --> 01:06:19,458
This dog's been on TV.

736
01:06:19,541 --> 01:06:21,333
He's worth more than you!

737
01:06:21,416 --> 01:06:23,125
You're going to pay for it, bitch.

738
01:06:23,791 --> 01:06:25,375
Come!

739
01:06:28,166 --> 01:06:29,958
What are you going to do?

740
01:06:45,916 --> 01:06:47,000
It fucking hurts!

741
01:06:55,208 --> 01:06:56,208
Son of a bitch!

742
01:06:57,166 --> 01:06:58,333
Namcha!

743
01:06:58,416 --> 01:06:59,708
Brownie, quickly!

744
01:07:00,250 --> 01:07:01,416
Stop!

745
01:07:17,125 --> 01:07:19,541
Inside, quickly!

746
01:07:28,500 --> 01:07:30,125
Good boy, Brownie.

747
01:07:30,208 --> 01:07:32,250
You're so brave.

748
01:07:33,083 --> 01:07:35,250
Thank you.

749
01:07:38,291 --> 01:07:39,958
Ladies and gentlemen!

750
01:07:40,041 --> 01:07:42,375
Get ready for the thrill of your life.

751
01:07:42,458 --> 01:07:45,583
The most dangerous act of the night!

752
01:08:21,125 --> 01:08:22,416
It's a dog!

753
01:08:22,500 --> 01:08:24,666
Dog!

754
01:08:26,916 --> 01:08:28,583
Brownie!

755
01:08:33,916 --> 01:08:36,166
Brownie…

756
01:08:59,041 --> 01:09:00,416
It's okay.

757
01:09:01,666 --> 01:09:03,125
Hey!

758
01:09:05,583 --> 01:09:06,833
You!

759
01:09:06,916 --> 01:09:08,166
Catch her!

760
01:09:08,250 --> 01:09:09,666
She's a thief!

761
01:09:14,208 --> 01:09:15,208
What did you steal?

762
01:09:18,500 --> 01:09:19,625
Brownie!

763
01:09:21,958 --> 01:09:22,791
Fuck!

764
01:09:25,125 --> 01:09:26,500
You've got to be kidding me.

765
01:09:27,291 --> 01:09:28,333
Move.

766
01:09:31,583 --> 01:09:34,000
Hey! The dog!

767
01:09:34,083 --> 01:09:36,375
Your dog went that way!

768
01:09:36,458 --> 01:09:38,708
That way! Quick!

769
01:09:39,791 --> 01:09:40,916
Out of the way!

770
01:09:43,125 --> 01:09:44,375
Brownie!

771
01:09:45,458 --> 01:09:48,958
-Sir! They went that way!
-Sir! That way!

772
01:09:49,041 --> 01:09:50,500
-That way!
-This way?

773
01:09:50,583 --> 01:09:52,041
Yes!

774
01:09:53,416 --> 01:09:54,291
Brownie!

775
01:09:58,583 --> 01:09:59,500
Brownie!

776
01:10:00,958 --> 01:10:01,833
Brownie!

777
01:10:18,458 --> 01:10:19,416
Brownie.

778
01:10:30,666 --> 01:10:32,125
Kitty cat.

779
01:10:32,916 --> 01:10:34,750
Have you seen a dog around here?

780
01:10:37,666 --> 01:10:39,333
Can you please help me find him?

781
01:11:29,333 --> 01:11:30,291
Brownie!

782
01:11:32,666 --> 01:11:33,916
Brownie!

783
01:11:35,791 --> 01:11:38,375
Why are you swimming here?

784
01:11:48,708 --> 01:11:49,666
Brownie.

785
01:11:50,541 --> 01:11:52,916
I thought I'd lost you!

786
01:12:21,291 --> 01:12:22,958
<i>Still got the nerve to call?</i>

787
01:12:24,333 --> 01:12:25,791
Can we talk nicely?

788
01:12:26,666 --> 01:12:27,750
Please?

789
01:12:28,500 --> 01:12:30,416
Just let us go.

790
01:12:31,291 --> 01:12:32,916
<i>I can let you go.</i>

791
01:12:33,541 --> 01:12:35,250
<i>But not the dog.</i>

792
01:12:39,375 --> 01:12:41,625
Can you be kind to the dogs?

793
01:12:45,125 --> 01:12:47,083
Little doggy.

794
01:12:47,166 --> 01:12:49,583
Little doggy.

795
01:12:53,041 --> 01:12:54,375
Handsome boy.

796
01:12:55,000 --> 01:12:56,541
<i>Kindness doesn't make money.</i>

797
01:12:57,875 --> 01:13:00,666
<i>Do you know</i>
<i>how much money I make from him?</i>

798
01:13:03,041 --> 01:13:04,666
<i>I'll give you one last chance.</i>

799
01:13:06,791 --> 01:13:08,375
<i>Bring me Gohan.</i>

800
01:13:11,625 --> 01:13:14,875
<i>I'll give you sixty grand and your permit.</i>

801
01:13:23,666 --> 01:13:24,666
<i>Choose wisely.</i>

802
01:13:25,375 --> 01:13:27,708
<i>It's your life or the dog's.</i>

803
01:13:28,750 --> 01:13:30,291
<i>What's it going to be?</i>

804
01:13:35,083 --> 01:13:36,208
This one.

805
01:13:39,958 --> 01:13:40,958
Thank you.

806
01:14:11,958 --> 01:14:13,333
This bracelet

807
01:14:15,750 --> 01:14:18,333
was given to me by my mom.

808
01:14:19,916 --> 01:14:21,833
She said it would keep me safe.

809
01:14:32,000 --> 01:14:33,083
I hope…

810
01:14:35,250 --> 01:14:36,500
that it will…

811
01:14:39,583 --> 01:14:42,000
keep you safe too, Brownie.

812
01:14:51,666 --> 01:14:53,750
Actually, my name isn't Namcha.

813
01:14:56,666 --> 01:14:57,916
It's Aye Shin.

814
01:15:02,583 --> 01:15:03,875
Please remember my name.

815
01:15:16,833 --> 01:15:18,125
And you…

816
01:15:21,041 --> 01:15:23,666
You'll be my Brownie forever.

817
01:15:24,291 --> 01:15:25,250
Okay?

818
01:15:53,708 --> 01:15:54,916
I got you a cake.

819
01:16:17,083 --> 01:16:21,000
Sorry that I could only
bring you this far.

820
01:16:57,250 --> 01:16:58,125
Hey!

821
01:16:59,125 --> 01:17:00,208
Where's the fucking dog?

822
01:17:03,791 --> 01:17:08,041
Far away from scums like you!

823
01:17:10,833 --> 01:17:11,708
Shit.

824
01:17:13,125 --> 01:17:14,500
Hey! Stop the train!

825
01:17:16,583 --> 01:17:17,583
Wait!

826
01:17:19,583 --> 01:17:20,458
Shit!

827
01:17:22,041 --> 01:17:22,916
Fuck!

828
01:17:27,083 --> 01:17:28,166
Is this what you want?

829
01:17:28,250 --> 01:17:30,750
You think you've won by freeing the dog?

830
01:17:31,375 --> 01:17:32,833
Are you stupid?

831
01:17:33,458 --> 01:17:36,416
There are thousands of strays
in this country.

832
01:17:36,500 --> 01:17:39,500
I can round them up, sedate them,
and make my living!

833
01:17:39,583 --> 01:17:40,541
But for you?

834
01:17:40,625 --> 01:17:41,958
You're done.

835
01:17:42,625 --> 01:17:46,000
I'll call immigration
and have you deported.

836
01:17:48,125 --> 01:17:49,583
Too late for that.

837
01:17:55,375 --> 01:17:56,375
{\an8}Found them.

838
01:17:59,500 --> 01:18:00,875
Fine.

839
01:18:00,958 --> 01:18:02,625
Let's see who they'll believe.

840
01:18:05,333 --> 01:18:06,416
I'm not scared of you.

841
01:18:13,000 --> 01:18:14,500
Wait!

842
01:18:14,583 --> 01:18:16,666
Listen to me. Wait.

843
01:18:16,750 --> 01:18:19,583
I have sixty grand.

844
01:18:19,666 --> 01:18:20,666
Your permit too.

845
01:18:20,750 --> 01:18:21,958
Please stop!

846
01:18:22,041 --> 01:18:23,041
I'm sorry.

847
01:18:24,458 --> 01:18:26,333
I won't do it again, okay?

848
01:18:26,416 --> 01:18:28,291
Just don't post the clip online.

849
01:18:32,125 --> 01:18:33,000
Dum.

850
01:18:40,583 --> 01:18:42,083
Lucky.

851
01:18:42,958 --> 01:18:43,875
Shabu.

852
01:18:45,166 --> 01:18:46,166
<i>Sugar.</i>

853
01:18:46,833 --> 01:18:47,833
<i>Kaowpun.</i>

854
01:18:48,458 --> 01:18:49,833
<i>Michael.</i>

855
01:18:52,291 --> 01:18:56,083
I know I can't rescue every dog
in this world.

856
01:18:56,791 --> 01:19:00,041
But at least I've rescued them from you.

857
01:19:00,125 --> 01:19:01,500
This is the best I can do.

858
01:19:29,083 --> 01:19:30,708
Was it you who called us?

859
01:19:32,208 --> 01:19:34,166
She said you hired illegal workers.

860
01:19:34,250 --> 01:19:35,666
<i>We'll talk at the station.</i>

861
01:19:39,291 --> 01:19:40,875
Do you have any other evidence?

862
01:19:42,125 --> 01:19:43,208
No.

863
01:19:44,291 --> 01:19:45,875
<i>Are you stupid?</i>

864
01:19:46,666 --> 01:19:49,666
<i>There are thousands of strays</i>
<i>in this country.</i>

865
01:19:50,416 --> 01:19:52,541
We can't do anything further.

866
01:19:53,583 --> 01:19:55,458
And you still have to be deported.

867
01:20:02,125 --> 01:20:05,083
BROWNIE

868
01:20:08,458 --> 01:20:12,125
<i>To whoever reads this letter…</i>

869
01:20:19,625 --> 01:20:23,583
<i>You've finally met this troublemaker.</i>

870
01:20:30,000 --> 01:20:31,666
<i>He's a good dog</i>

871
01:20:33,125 --> 01:20:35,250
<i>who deserves a good life.</i>

872
01:20:36,458 --> 01:20:39,083
<i>A life that I can't give.</i>

873
01:20:48,333 --> 01:20:51,208
<i>You may not love him.</i>

874
01:20:52,500 --> 01:20:55,166
<i>But please don't hurt him.</i>

875
01:20:57,083 --> 01:21:02,125
<i>Let him have a little space</i>
<i>to live in this world.</i>

876
01:21:06,000 --> 01:21:08,416
<i>But if you love him…</i>

877
01:21:08,500 --> 01:21:10,708
BROWNIE

878
01:21:10,791 --> 01:21:13,625
<i>It doesn't matter what his name was.</i>

879
01:21:19,666 --> 01:21:25,708
<i>Just give him one last name</i>
<i>for the rest of his life.</i>

880
01:23:23,833 --> 01:23:26,333
You can do it. It's not that much.

881
01:23:26,916 --> 01:23:28,541
I'm worried I won't finish in time.

882
01:23:29,583 --> 01:23:30,583
Let's go, Pelé.

883
01:23:33,125 --> 01:23:34,291
Wait.

884
01:23:35,166 --> 01:23:36,625
Take a photo of me with this dog.

885
01:23:36,708 --> 01:23:37,833
Stop fooling around.

886
01:23:37,916 --> 01:23:39,583
Gosh, you're so cute!

887
01:23:47,541 --> 01:23:50,250
Polaroids are expensive, you know?

888
01:23:50,333 --> 01:23:51,666
Why do you want a photo with the dog?

889
01:23:51,750 --> 01:23:54,125
The dog is here to welcome us,

890
01:23:54,208 --> 01:23:55,833
which means today will be a good day.

891
01:23:55,916 --> 01:23:57,791
I will ace my interview exam.

892
01:23:58,500 --> 01:24:00,416
It's for good luck.

893
01:24:02,750 --> 01:24:04,708
Look over there.

894
01:24:20,291 --> 01:24:22,833
{\an8}PELÉ & JAIDEE 4EVERRR!

895
01:24:24,583 --> 01:24:26,166
That's cringe, man!

896
01:24:27,083 --> 01:24:28,916
No one is allowed to see this.

897
01:24:29,000 --> 01:24:32,833
You got Pelé in a photo with me.

898
01:24:32,916 --> 01:24:35,708
If I get into university,
I'll play with you every day.

899
01:24:35,791 --> 01:24:36,666
Okay?

900
01:24:37,291 --> 01:24:39,541
Okay.

901
01:24:40,416 --> 01:24:41,458
Pelé.

902
01:24:41,541 --> 01:24:42,458
Can you name him?

903
01:24:47,708 --> 01:24:48,625
Whitey.

904
01:24:48,708 --> 01:24:49,833
Oh, come on!

905
01:24:49,916 --> 01:24:51,041
Can you be more creative?

906
01:24:52,708 --> 01:24:53,791
Elsa.

907
01:24:54,500 --> 01:24:55,375
Elsa?

908
01:24:55,458 --> 01:24:56,916
Elsa!

909
01:24:57,000 --> 01:24:58,250
Elsa?

910
01:24:58,333 --> 01:25:01,041
Well, it's white,
so she's a snow princess.

911
01:25:01,125 --> 01:25:03,333
What kind of princess has a ding dong?

912
01:25:05,041 --> 01:25:06,500
Hima sounds better.

913
01:25:07,333 --> 01:25:09,416
-Is it?
-Let's go. Everybody's gone.

914
01:25:10,958 --> 01:25:12,083
See you around, Hima.

915
01:25:21,125 --> 01:25:23,250
Welcome, Fine Arts freshmen!

916
01:25:23,333 --> 01:25:26,333
Hop off the train and line up over here.

917
01:25:26,416 --> 01:25:28,958
Follow your seniors.

918
01:25:29,041 --> 01:25:30,000
Pelé.

919
01:25:31,333 --> 01:25:32,250
There's Hima.

920
01:25:39,708 --> 01:25:44,583
HIMA

921
01:25:48,333 --> 01:25:49,250
Hima!

922
01:25:50,083 --> 01:25:51,416
Do you know your name yet?

923
01:25:51,500 --> 01:25:53,333
I brought you some apples.

924
01:25:53,416 --> 01:25:55,375
Helps with digestion.

925
01:25:55,458 --> 01:25:57,583
Dig in.

926
01:25:57,666 --> 01:26:00,291
-Jaidee, everybody's left already.
-Here.

927
01:26:00,375 --> 01:26:01,791
-Quick!
-And some water.

928
01:26:02,791 --> 01:26:03,666
Wait a second!

929
01:26:04,791 --> 01:26:07,250
Since we're already feeding him every day,

930
01:26:08,541 --> 01:26:11,375
shall we raise him at our rental house?

931
01:26:12,500 --> 01:26:13,500
Shall we?

932
01:26:15,583 --> 01:26:17,125
He doesn't even know his name.

933
01:26:17,708 --> 01:26:19,791
Playing with him is enough.

934
01:26:20,583 --> 01:26:21,958
He'll just be a burden.

935
01:26:22,833 --> 01:26:24,541
-Let's go home.
-Let's go.

936
01:26:27,750 --> 01:26:30,333
We do everything as a couple,

937
01:26:30,416 --> 01:26:33,000
but you never want
to admit our relationship.

938
01:26:33,083 --> 01:26:35,916
Why is it so hard for you?

939
01:26:36,833 --> 01:26:38,625
I don't want to put a label on it.

940
01:26:39,666 --> 01:26:41,250
Or should we just call it off?

941
01:26:42,250 --> 01:26:43,250
So childish!

942
01:26:43,833 --> 01:26:44,833
Pelé!

943
01:27:00,250 --> 01:27:01,500
Hima.

944
01:27:01,583 --> 01:27:02,708
I've graduated.

945
01:27:04,083 --> 01:27:06,291
I won't be around as often now.

946
01:27:06,958 --> 01:27:09,041
I hope you'll meet kind people.

947
01:27:11,375 --> 01:27:12,916
You're really going to leave?

948
01:27:14,041 --> 01:27:15,125
Without a word?

949
01:27:17,416 --> 01:27:18,458
I'm sorry, okay?

950
01:27:24,083 --> 01:27:24,958
Jaidee!

951
01:27:27,833 --> 01:27:29,416
Can we talk?

952
01:27:30,291 --> 01:27:31,250
Jaidee!

953
01:28:06,916 --> 01:28:09,500
-This camera right here.
-Thank you.

954
01:28:09,583 --> 01:28:11,916
One, two, three.

955
01:28:12,000 --> 01:28:14,375
One more. One, two, three.

956
01:28:15,041 --> 01:28:17,375
Thank you.

957
01:28:23,916 --> 01:28:25,083
Help me out.

958
01:28:26,416 --> 01:28:27,750
Call your mom.

959
01:28:40,041 --> 01:28:41,291
Hima!

960
01:28:43,250 --> 01:28:47,208
-Hima…
-Hima…

961
01:28:47,291 --> 01:28:49,125
Here!

962
01:28:49,208 --> 01:28:51,041
Good boy.

963
01:28:52,416 --> 01:28:53,791
Hima.

964
01:28:53,875 --> 01:28:56,041
Good boy.

965
01:28:58,666 --> 01:28:59,791
How's it going?

966
01:29:03,125 --> 01:29:04,625
I've missed you.

967
01:29:08,083 --> 01:29:10,750
How about a group photo?

968
01:29:10,833 --> 01:29:12,333
-Okay.
-Scooch in!

969
01:29:12,416 --> 01:29:13,750
-Ready?
-Look there.

970
01:29:13,833 --> 01:29:15,041
-One…
-The camera over there.

971
01:29:15,125 --> 01:29:16,125
Wait!

972
01:29:16,208 --> 01:29:17,541
Pelé, join us.

973
01:29:19,541 --> 01:29:22,541
The professor didn't let you graduate,
but I will.

974
01:29:22,625 --> 01:29:23,916
Come on, man!

975
01:29:26,791 --> 01:29:28,000
Squat in the front.

976
01:29:28,083 --> 01:29:29,333
Ready, guys?

977
01:29:29,416 --> 01:29:30,916
Get closer. Ready?

978
01:29:31,000 --> 01:29:32,625
Three, two, one.

979
01:29:32,708 --> 01:29:33,750
How's it going?

980
01:29:34,583 --> 01:29:35,750
You're a flight attendant now?

981
01:29:37,625 --> 01:29:38,583
Congratulations.

982
01:29:46,166 --> 01:29:47,083
Pelé.

983
01:29:47,166 --> 01:29:50,375
You should move to the side, man.

984
01:29:50,458 --> 01:29:53,833
Your hair is stealing our moment.

985
01:29:55,208 --> 01:29:57,875
Okay. That's perfect, everyone!

986
01:29:57,958 --> 01:29:58,916
Okay.

987
01:29:59,000 --> 01:29:59,875
Jaidee.

988
01:29:59,958 --> 01:30:01,750
Come on. Over here.

989
01:30:01,833 --> 01:30:04,291
I realized I can't be without you.

990
01:30:08,125 --> 01:30:10,250
I'm ready to make it official now.

991
01:30:14,000 --> 01:30:15,375
I also realized

992
01:30:15,458 --> 01:30:17,500
that my life is way better without you.

993
01:30:20,458 --> 01:30:21,666
Please.

994
01:30:21,750 --> 01:30:22,833
Can you just…

995
01:30:23,583 --> 01:30:24,791
leave me alone?

996
01:30:26,125 --> 01:30:28,125
Okay, let's take the photo.

997
01:30:28,208 --> 01:30:29,416
The sun is setting.

998
01:30:29,500 --> 01:30:31,333
Come on, guys. Ready?

999
01:30:31,416 --> 01:30:33,750
One, two, three!

1000
01:30:36,125 --> 01:30:37,125
Hima!

1001
01:30:38,333 --> 01:30:41,458
He only got a small stitch today.

1002
01:30:42,750 --> 01:30:44,708
But the bad news is…

1003
01:30:45,500 --> 01:30:47,666
He may not live much longer.

1004
01:30:50,541 --> 01:30:52,583
There's nothing wrong with his leg,

1005
01:30:52,666 --> 01:30:55,083
but his kidneys are in poor condition.

1006
01:30:55,875 --> 01:30:59,291
He needs to be on a strict diet.

1007
01:30:59,375 --> 01:31:01,750
No human food whatsoever.

1008
01:31:01,833 --> 01:31:04,333
He needs constant saline shots

1009
01:31:04,416 --> 01:31:07,625
to dilute the waste from his blood.

1010
01:31:09,708 --> 01:31:10,625
So…

1011
01:31:11,708 --> 01:31:13,541
How much time does he have left?

1012
01:31:15,416 --> 01:31:16,666
For him…

1013
01:31:17,500 --> 01:31:20,166
Around three months.

1014
01:31:21,625 --> 01:31:23,250
Who is he living with?

1015
01:31:23,333 --> 01:31:24,583
Who's taking care of him?

1016
01:31:33,625 --> 01:31:34,666
He's with me.

1017
01:31:37,791 --> 01:31:39,541
I'm the only one who's still around.

1018
01:31:42,916 --> 01:31:44,625
Okay, so listen.

1019
01:31:45,500 --> 01:31:48,375
What you need to do

1020
01:31:48,458 --> 01:31:51,541
is give him saline shots
at least three days a week.

1021
01:31:51,625 --> 01:31:53,291
Be gentle.

1022
01:31:53,375 --> 01:31:55,666
He's probably ten years old now.

1023
01:31:56,583 --> 01:31:58,000
Take good care of him.

1024
01:31:59,125 --> 01:32:01,208
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

1025
01:32:01,291 --> 01:32:02,500
Thank you.

1026
01:32:03,750 --> 01:32:05,291
We'll handle the bill.

1027
01:32:05,375 --> 01:32:06,875
You two stay with Hima.

1028
01:32:08,833 --> 01:32:10,125
See you.

1029
01:32:17,666 --> 01:32:19,166
Give me the medicine.

1030
01:32:19,250 --> 01:32:20,208
I'll handle it.

1031
01:32:20,291 --> 01:32:23,375
It's a two-person job.

1032
01:32:24,125 --> 01:32:25,500
Didn't you see it?

1033
01:32:26,791 --> 01:32:27,916
What are you saying?

1034
01:32:29,125 --> 01:32:30,000
I mean…

1035
01:32:31,000 --> 01:32:34,958
We can do it at the station together.

1036
01:32:50,916 --> 01:32:52,125
Wait here.

1037
01:32:53,041 --> 01:32:54,541
Look out for your mom.

1038
01:32:56,875 --> 01:32:59,958
Pelé, what a life you're living.

1039
01:33:00,041 --> 01:33:03,500
All you do is sit around,
watching trains go by.

1040
01:33:03,583 --> 01:33:06,666
Since you've dropped out,
what are you doing now?

1041
01:33:06,750 --> 01:33:08,291
I'm waiting for Jaidee.

1042
01:33:09,708 --> 01:33:11,750
I'm guarding my dog! God, you're nosy!

1043
01:33:12,500 --> 01:33:13,833
Then where's your dog?

1044
01:33:16,708 --> 01:33:18,000
Hey.

1045
01:33:18,083 --> 01:33:19,375
Hima!

1046
01:33:19,458 --> 01:33:20,333
Hima!

1047
01:33:28,333 --> 01:33:30,166
What are the chances
of an old, partially blind dog

1048
01:33:30,250 --> 01:33:32,208
getting hit while crossing the road?

1049
01:33:32,291 --> 01:33:33,250
<i>100% instant death.</i>

1050
01:33:36,583 --> 01:33:37,458
Hima!

1051
01:33:40,333 --> 01:33:42,708
Are you trying to cross the road
or cross into the next life?

1052
01:33:54,458 --> 01:33:55,458
Eat up.

1053
01:34:01,291 --> 01:34:02,875
Turn it down a notch.

1054
01:34:03,833 --> 01:34:05,250
Do us all a favor.

1055
01:34:15,000 --> 01:34:16,083
I'm out.

1056
01:34:17,416 --> 01:34:19,541
Don't bother waiting.
Your mom isn't coming.

1057
01:34:51,583 --> 01:34:52,875
I'm picking up Hima

1058
01:34:55,250 --> 01:34:56,916
and moving back into the house.

1059
01:34:59,125 --> 01:35:01,291
It's best to take care of him there.

1060
01:35:02,875 --> 01:35:04,500
For his last three months,

1061
01:35:06,375 --> 01:35:08,333
I want to treat him well.

1062
01:35:08,875 --> 01:35:10,500
I didn't do enough before.

1063
01:35:13,041 --> 01:35:14,750
This is my only chance.

1064
01:35:28,833 --> 01:35:30,458
Excited to come home?

1065
01:35:30,541 --> 01:35:32,291
Don't rush.

1066
01:35:32,375 --> 01:35:33,583
Let me park.

1067
01:35:33,666 --> 01:35:35,458
Be patient.

1068
01:35:36,666 --> 01:35:37,958
Easy, boss.

1069
01:35:45,541 --> 01:35:48,125
Watch your step, old man!

1070
01:35:52,625 --> 01:35:54,000
It's okay. Let me take that.

1071
01:36:11,958 --> 01:36:13,208
All done.

1072
01:36:13,291 --> 01:36:15,666
Now you smell nice and clean!

1073
01:36:19,375 --> 01:36:20,541
Wow, thanks for that.

1074
01:36:22,958 --> 01:36:25,250
How about a reward after your shower?

1075
01:36:25,333 --> 01:36:26,583
You want some milk, Hima?

1076
01:36:27,291 --> 01:36:28,666
Dogs can't have dairy.

1077
01:36:28,750 --> 01:36:30,000
Didn't you know?

1078
01:36:39,416 --> 01:36:41,791
Who's a handsome boy?

1079
01:36:43,708 --> 01:36:47,541
HIMA

1080
01:36:47,625 --> 01:36:49,333
I drew that for him.

1081
01:36:49,416 --> 01:36:52,291
I listened to a lot of metal
while you were gone.

1082
01:36:52,375 --> 01:36:53,666
Can't really do slow songs.

1083
01:36:53,750 --> 01:36:56,166
They trigger the waterworks.

1084
01:36:56,250 --> 01:36:58,666
I needed something heavier.
Like I was back in the day.

1085
01:36:58,750 --> 01:36:59,916
-A sweet face, but--
-I don't like it.

1086
01:37:00,000 --> 01:37:01,375
Okay, ma'am.

1087
01:37:06,125 --> 01:37:08,833
{\an8}HIMA

1088
01:37:17,000 --> 01:37:20,208
You won't feel a thing.

1089
01:37:20,291 --> 01:37:21,875
Stay still.

1090
01:37:29,541 --> 01:37:30,791
Got it.

1091
01:37:31,833 --> 01:37:32,916
Good boy.

1092
01:37:34,666 --> 01:37:36,750
I'm scheduled to fly almost every day.

1093
01:37:36,833 --> 01:37:38,833
I'll swap flights for these three months,

1094
01:37:38,916 --> 01:37:41,625
so I can help with Hima.

1095
01:37:41,708 --> 01:37:43,541
So which days are you busy?

1096
01:37:49,333 --> 01:37:50,416
Actually…

1097
01:37:52,083 --> 01:37:54,083
My mom doesn't know that I've dropped out.

1098
01:37:58,583 --> 01:38:00,791
I told her I'm doing my master's,

1099
01:38:01,875 --> 01:38:03,541
so I could use the tuition money.

1100
01:38:07,250 --> 01:38:08,416
So you're free every day.

1101
01:38:10,250 --> 01:38:13,291
You do lunch.
I'll do breakfast and dinner.

1102
01:38:13,875 --> 01:38:15,916
I'll write down the feeding times for you.

1103
01:38:17,125 --> 01:38:18,291
Sounds good, Hima?

1104
01:38:18,375 --> 01:38:20,416
Almost done.

1105
01:38:21,333 --> 01:38:22,750
What a good boy.

1106
01:38:25,666 --> 01:38:27,333
It's a crisis.

1107
01:38:27,875 --> 01:38:30,041
<i>You're in a hopeless situation.</i>

1108
01:38:30,125 --> 01:38:32,166
<i>The fact that she doesn't care</i>

1109
01:38:32,250 --> 01:38:34,291
<i>means that she feels nothing</i>
<i>for you anymore.</i>

1110
01:38:36,041 --> 01:38:37,708
Let me tell you something.

1111
01:38:37,791 --> 01:38:40,583
My husband cheated on me three times.

1112
01:38:40,666 --> 01:38:43,250
Guess how I felt the third time.

1113
01:38:44,625 --> 01:38:45,708
Hatred?

1114
01:38:47,125 --> 01:38:48,625
I felt nothing.

1115
01:38:50,208 --> 01:38:52,666
You know, the opposite of love

1116
01:38:52,750 --> 01:38:54,208
isn't hate.

1117
01:38:54,875 --> 01:38:57,708
It's feeling nothing.

1118
01:39:06,250 --> 01:39:09,583
What if I treat Hima well
before he passes?

1119
01:39:09,666 --> 01:39:11,458
Will Jaidee see me differently?

1120
01:39:11,541 --> 01:39:14,541
<i>That sounds fake as hell, man.</i>

1121
01:39:14,625 --> 01:39:17,458
<i>Everyone can see</i>
<i>that you're not a dog person.</i>

1122
01:39:17,541 --> 01:39:19,125
<i>And don't forget to pay me.</i>

1123
01:39:19,208 --> 01:39:21,458
<i>You've used up this month's credits.</i>

1124
01:39:21,541 --> 01:39:23,750
Gosh, Pelé.

1125
01:39:23,833 --> 01:39:25,833
You're unbelievable.

1126
01:39:25,916 --> 01:39:28,416
You can't even afford
your AI subscription.

1127
01:39:28,500 --> 01:39:30,375
How are you going
to pay my rent this month?

1128
01:39:30,458 --> 01:39:32,166
Well, help me think!

1129
01:39:34,375 --> 01:39:37,750
If she agrees to move back in with me,
I'll keep paying your rent.

1130
01:39:38,375 --> 01:39:40,166
Fine!

1131
01:39:40,875 --> 01:39:44,125
Look. Don't pretend to love dogs.

1132
01:39:44,208 --> 01:39:46,708
You just have to prove to her

1133
01:39:46,791 --> 01:39:48,375
that the dog loves you!

1134
01:39:53,625 --> 01:39:55,375
See you soon, buddy.

1135
01:39:55,458 --> 01:39:57,708
Be a good boy, okay?

1136
01:39:57,791 --> 01:39:58,750
I'll hurry back.

1137
01:39:58,833 --> 01:40:00,458
Take care of the house.

1138
01:40:06,333 --> 01:40:07,458
See you, Jaidee.

1139
01:40:10,208 --> 01:40:11,291
Got everything, right?

1140
01:40:19,416 --> 01:40:21,041
You want this?

1141
01:40:21,125 --> 01:40:21,958
What do you do?

1142
01:40:24,083 --> 01:40:25,333
Paw.

1143
01:40:27,666 --> 01:40:30,041
Good boy!

1144
01:40:30,125 --> 01:40:31,000
For you.

1145
01:40:33,166 --> 01:40:34,875
I'm the pack leader.

1146
01:40:34,958 --> 01:40:35,833
Remember that.

1147
01:40:59,291 --> 01:41:00,583
Jaidee.

1148
01:41:00,666 --> 01:41:01,541
Jaidee.

1149
01:41:05,333 --> 01:41:07,166
He just crashed in my room.

1150
01:41:11,708 --> 01:41:12,625
Take care of him.

1151
01:41:13,791 --> 01:41:14,666
Night.

1152
01:41:20,833 --> 01:41:21,750
Hima.

1153
01:41:21,833 --> 01:41:22,833
What's wrong?

1154
01:41:23,625 --> 01:41:25,083
Was it a nightmare?

1155
01:41:25,166 --> 01:41:26,958
It's okay.

1156
01:41:36,041 --> 01:41:39,333
Pelé, do you think Jaidee's lost it?

1157
01:41:40,375 --> 01:41:41,291
Look at her.

1158
01:41:47,958 --> 01:41:51,208
She's working out. Let her be!

1159
01:41:54,916 --> 01:41:56,125
You good, bro?

1160
01:41:56,208 --> 01:41:57,833
Still jumpy, Scooby Doo?

1161
01:42:00,875 --> 01:42:02,958
Where's your Shaggy gone?

1162
01:42:03,041 --> 01:42:05,083
Can you not play horror games with Hima?

1163
01:42:05,708 --> 01:42:07,291
He gets nightmares.

1164
01:42:07,958 --> 01:42:08,916
You guys too.

1165
01:42:09,000 --> 01:42:11,416
If you're here just to mess with Hima,
don't come again.

1166
01:42:12,291 --> 01:42:14,166
Hima. Lunch.

1167
01:42:17,958 --> 01:42:19,083
Hima.

1168
01:42:19,166 --> 01:42:20,083
Come here.

1169
01:42:20,166 --> 01:42:21,416
Have your lunch with me.

1170
01:42:23,458 --> 01:42:25,000
Hima, lunch.

1171
01:42:39,541 --> 01:42:40,541
Jaidee.

1172
01:42:43,208 --> 01:42:44,125
I think we have a problem.

1173
01:42:44,750 --> 01:42:46,000
He's really attached to me.

1174
01:42:46,083 --> 01:42:48,000
I think he wants me to sleep in your room.

1175
01:42:48,083 --> 01:42:49,250
Maybe it's a good idea.

1176
01:42:49,333 --> 01:42:51,833
Shall we try it? Is there enough room?

1177
01:43:00,083 --> 01:43:01,333
He sure is attached.

1178
01:43:05,166 --> 01:43:06,583
I can sleep on the floor.

1179
01:43:22,916 --> 01:43:24,666
You're all done. Good boy.

1180
01:43:24,750 --> 01:43:26,666
Bang, bang! You're dead!

1181
01:43:28,791 --> 01:43:29,750
Awesome.

1182
01:43:30,416 --> 01:43:31,833
RIP, Hima.

1183
01:43:34,500 --> 01:43:36,791
Can you not joke about death with him?

1184
01:43:37,958 --> 01:43:40,250
You know he doesn't have much time.

1185
01:43:44,541 --> 01:43:46,375
I was just joking.

1186
01:43:49,583 --> 01:43:50,541
Are you mad?

1187
01:43:53,208 --> 01:43:54,083
I don't like it.

1188
01:43:57,791 --> 01:43:58,666
Pelé!

1189
01:44:00,250 --> 01:44:01,375
Let me see.

1190
01:44:02,041 --> 01:44:05,041
Please wait 15 minutes to observe,
then you can go home.

1191
01:44:16,958 --> 01:44:18,500
Please don't hate him.

1192
01:44:19,875 --> 01:44:21,291
He didn't mean it.

1193
01:44:22,916 --> 01:44:24,166
I don't hate him.

1194
01:44:25,041 --> 01:44:27,250
He still bites hard. That's healthy.

1195
01:44:32,916 --> 01:44:34,583
You can hate me if you want.

1196
01:44:41,375 --> 01:44:43,416
Just don't feel nothing.

1197
01:44:54,250 --> 01:44:56,125
Let me hate you for now.

1198
01:45:08,208 --> 01:45:09,083
Bang!

1199
01:45:12,791 --> 01:45:13,625
You're dead.

1200
01:45:22,500 --> 01:45:23,500
Oh, that hurts!

1201
01:45:27,458 --> 01:45:28,458
Paw.

1202
01:45:45,875 --> 01:45:47,458
I did it in a hurry.

1203
01:45:48,291 --> 01:45:49,583
ART CLASSES BY PELÉ

1204
01:45:49,666 --> 01:45:53,458
You'd probably do a better job than I do.

1205
01:45:56,333 --> 01:45:58,541
Stop lying to your mom for her money.

1206
01:46:17,875 --> 01:46:18,958
Pelé.

1207
01:46:22,083 --> 01:46:24,041
It's been a month together with Hima.

1208
01:46:30,416 --> 01:46:32,958
Will this be a monthly thing now?

1209
01:46:33,041 --> 01:46:33,916
Yes.

1210
01:46:35,000 --> 01:46:37,541
Let's stay together for a long time, Hima.

1211
01:46:37,625 --> 01:46:38,916
I've read this somewhere.

1212
01:46:39,000 --> 01:46:41,750
They say when dogs get a lot of love,

1213
01:46:41,833 --> 01:46:43,833
they live longer.

1214
01:46:45,166 --> 01:46:46,291
That's touching.

1215
01:46:47,541 --> 01:46:48,416
Isn't it, boss?

1216
01:46:48,500 --> 01:46:49,833
Very touching.

1217
01:46:50,458 --> 01:46:52,333
Cut the cake already!

1218
01:46:55,166 --> 01:46:56,708
Just use your hands.

1219
01:47:03,833 --> 01:47:04,875
What flavor is this?

1220
01:47:06,083 --> 01:47:07,375
Liver.

1221
01:47:15,291 --> 01:47:17,541
That little glutton's stealing your food.

1222
01:47:18,166 --> 01:47:20,333
Why didn't you tell me?

1223
01:47:22,916 --> 01:47:24,750
Hima, can I have a bite?

1224
01:47:32,125 --> 01:47:33,750
Tastes pretty "ruff."

1225
01:47:41,791 --> 01:47:42,625
Were…

1226
01:47:43,875 --> 01:47:45,875
Were you always this sweet?

1227
01:47:57,208 --> 01:47:58,250
You just noticed?

1228
01:48:02,833 --> 01:48:03,916
Hima!

1229
01:48:04,000 --> 01:48:04,916
Eat up!

1230
01:48:05,583 --> 01:48:07,583
Birthday boy still hasn't had a bite.

1231
01:48:07,666 --> 01:48:09,958
-All yours.
-Do I need to feed him? Oh!

1232
01:48:16,750 --> 01:48:20,708
{\an8}FOOD/MEDICINE, SALINE

1233
01:48:36,833 --> 01:48:39,458
{\an8}FOOD/MEDICINE, SALINE (KIND DOC DAY),
MEAL TIME

1234
01:48:44,291 --> 01:48:45,291
Hima!

1235
01:49:14,041 --> 01:49:17,375
{\an8}<i>THE STORY OF AN OLD STRAY DOG</i>

1236
01:49:24,583 --> 01:49:26,875
<i>Once there lived an Old Dog,</i>

1237
01:49:26,958 --> 01:49:28,625
<i>who crossed the road recklessly.</i>

1238
01:49:29,750 --> 01:49:32,750
<i>He devoured leftovers</i>
<i>and ruined his health.</i>

1239
01:49:33,875 --> 01:49:36,750
<i>One day, he met a girl who loved him.</i>

1240
01:49:38,583 --> 01:49:41,500
<i>To make her truly happy,</i>

1241
01:49:41,583 --> 01:49:43,166
<i>he must live as long as possible.</i>

1242
01:49:46,208 --> 01:49:48,166
<i>But he's already so old.</i>

1243
01:49:48,250 --> 01:49:51,875
<i>So the Old Dog began</i>
<i>to take care of himself,</i>

1244
01:49:51,958 --> 01:49:54,250
<i>hoping to be with her</i>
<i>for a long, long time,</i>

1245
01:49:54,875 --> 01:49:58,416
<i>and to explore the world with her.</i>

1246
01:50:03,750 --> 01:50:05,791
<i>The Old Dog promised the girl,</i>

1247
01:50:06,416 --> 01:50:08,583
<i>"Until snow falls in Thailand,</i>

1248
01:50:08,666 --> 01:50:10,583
<i>I will never leave you."</i>

1249
01:50:20,166 --> 01:50:21,458
-Got it?
-Hang on.

1250
01:50:21,541 --> 01:50:23,333
-Okay?
-Okay.

1251
01:50:23,416 --> 01:50:24,916
No worries, Hima.

1252
01:50:25,666 --> 01:50:27,416
Let's go on an adventure!

1253
01:50:28,375 --> 01:50:29,208
Of course!

1254
01:50:29,291 --> 01:50:31,666
Your wish is granted.

1255
01:50:31,750 --> 01:50:33,208
Are you sure about that?

1256
01:50:33,291 --> 01:50:34,708
We can go every month.

1257
01:51:17,541 --> 01:51:18,708
Well done, Hima.

1258
01:51:21,708 --> 01:51:23,000
He trusts me now.

1259
01:51:24,416 --> 01:51:25,625
You won't have to worry anymore.

1260
01:51:27,583 --> 01:51:28,583
Good boy.

1261
01:51:29,583 --> 01:51:30,583
Pack leader.

1262
01:51:37,958 --> 01:51:39,500
I'm the pack leader now.

1263
01:51:49,250 --> 01:51:51,958
Too bad our time with him is so short.

1264
01:51:57,625 --> 01:52:00,541
Three months might feel long for a dog.

1265
01:52:01,333 --> 01:52:04,375
People and dogs
experience time differently.

1266
01:52:06,583 --> 01:52:09,416
Dogs are better than humans
at remembering certain details.

1267
01:52:10,666 --> 01:52:12,958
When someone treats them well,

1268
01:52:13,041 --> 01:52:15,541
time slows down.

1269
01:52:16,875 --> 01:52:17,875
That explains it.

1270
01:52:19,791 --> 01:52:21,375
Since you came back…

1271
01:52:23,458 --> 01:52:25,291
time barely moves.

1272
01:52:30,625 --> 01:52:33,000
Maybe I'm turning into a dog.

1273
01:52:41,625 --> 01:52:42,875
What do you think…

1274
01:52:44,750 --> 01:52:45,875
he dreams about?

1275
01:52:48,375 --> 01:52:49,583
Are you really dreaming?

1276
01:53:04,041 --> 01:53:05,041
Pelé.

1277
01:53:14,250 --> 01:53:15,250
Jaidee!

1278
01:53:16,583 --> 01:53:18,375
I want to go to the beach.

1279
01:53:20,291 --> 01:53:22,125
Take me to the beach, Mom!

1280
01:53:22,708 --> 01:53:23,791
Okay.

1281
01:53:23,875 --> 01:53:25,333
If Hima wants to go,

1282
01:53:26,125 --> 01:53:27,166
then why not?

1283
01:53:33,125 --> 01:53:35,083
-Look at the camera.
-Smile for the camera!

1284
01:53:35,166 --> 01:53:37,583
-One, two, three.
-Look.

1285
01:53:38,958 --> 01:53:42,000
Smile, old man! We're on vacation.

1286
01:53:42,875 --> 01:53:44,958
-Let's go to the beach today.
-Meatballs?

1287
01:53:46,541 --> 01:53:47,875
-Meatballs?
-A skewer, please.

1288
01:53:47,958 --> 01:53:50,416
Want some meatballs, Hima?

1289
01:53:51,708 --> 01:53:53,791
Can he eat that?

1290
01:53:54,750 --> 01:53:55,791
It's salty.

1291
01:53:58,916 --> 01:54:00,250
Come on, Pelé!

1292
01:54:00,333 --> 01:54:01,500
Not anymore.

1293
01:54:03,166 --> 01:54:04,375
Come on!

1294
01:54:04,458 --> 01:54:07,375
Who would want to eat that, right?

1295
01:54:12,583 --> 01:54:14,166
Quickly! The sun's going down, Hima.

1296
01:54:15,833 --> 01:54:19,208
-Look at the sea, Hima.
-Here it is!

1297
01:54:19,875 --> 01:54:21,208
First time, huh?

1298
01:54:22,791 --> 01:54:23,750
Isn't it pretty?

1299
01:54:37,125 --> 01:54:38,583
Hima, wait up!

1300
01:54:43,333 --> 01:54:45,166
-Wait!
-Hey!

1301
01:54:46,208 --> 01:54:47,208
Hima!

1302
01:54:48,083 --> 01:54:49,208
Wait for me!

1303
01:54:52,916 --> 01:54:53,958
How about that?

1304
01:54:57,625 --> 01:55:01,250
-We should take a walk here next time.
-I've played this at home before.

1305
01:55:01,333 --> 01:55:04,000
He's wiped out.

1306
01:55:04,083 --> 01:55:05,750
Sleeping like a log.

1307
01:55:18,166 --> 01:55:19,083
Jaidee.

1308
01:55:24,000 --> 01:55:26,541
You said Hima likes to dream.

1309
01:55:27,375 --> 01:55:28,666
I think I know what he dreams of.

1310
01:55:28,750 --> 01:55:30,083
What?

1311
01:55:49,625 --> 01:55:52,041
PELÉ & JAIDEE 4EVERRR!

1312
01:55:52,125 --> 01:55:53,291
He dreams of…

1313
01:55:56,083 --> 01:55:57,708
staying with us forever.

1314
01:56:05,458 --> 01:56:06,583
Jaidee.

1315
01:56:12,041 --> 01:56:13,000
Shall we…

1316
01:56:15,791 --> 01:56:17,166
be together for real?

1317
01:56:35,833 --> 01:56:37,583
Actually, apart from Hima…

1318
01:56:40,125 --> 01:56:41,541
I came back

1319
01:56:44,916 --> 01:56:46,333
because I was worried about you.

1320
01:56:51,750 --> 01:56:53,416
But I don't know if you've noticed.

1321
01:56:59,208 --> 01:57:01,750
I've been seeing someone for a while now.

1322
01:57:09,708 --> 01:57:11,250
I figured that

1323
01:57:13,458 --> 01:57:14,958
once Hima is gone,

1324
01:57:18,125 --> 01:57:19,916
I probably won't see you again.

1325
01:57:29,000 --> 01:57:30,958
But I don't hate you at all.

1326
01:57:35,208 --> 01:57:36,208
I just…

1327
01:57:38,500 --> 01:57:40,125
don't want the other person to wait.

1328
01:57:50,541 --> 01:57:51,416
Hey.

1329
01:57:53,125 --> 01:57:54,125
I get it.

1330
01:58:02,875 --> 01:58:07,666
HIMA

1331
01:59:01,375 --> 01:59:04,291
Hima, you haven't had your saline yet.

1332
01:59:04,375 --> 01:59:05,833
Let's give you some.

1333
01:59:12,458 --> 01:59:13,666
Just a second.

1334
01:59:49,000 --> 01:59:51,541
Why am I giving you this?

1335
01:59:53,208 --> 01:59:54,833
You'll die anyway.

1336
02:00:06,958 --> 02:00:07,875
Hima.

1337
02:00:10,708 --> 02:00:12,666
Can you live on a little longer?

1338
02:00:28,208 --> 02:00:29,083
Hima.

1339
02:00:35,375 --> 02:00:37,208
Can you not die?

1340
02:00:43,083 --> 02:00:45,375
I don't have anyone left.

1341
02:01:13,583 --> 02:01:17,083
PELÉ & JAIDEE 4EVERRR!

1342
02:02:14,041 --> 02:02:15,375
Still awake?

1343
02:02:34,625 --> 02:02:36,041
I'm sorry.

1344
02:02:39,500 --> 02:02:41,166
From now on…

1345
02:02:43,250 --> 02:02:46,208
I won't see you and Hima again.

1346
02:03:01,041 --> 02:03:03,583
If I keep seeing you both,

1347
02:03:07,125 --> 02:03:09,666
I might start loving you again.

1348
02:03:16,416 --> 02:03:17,416
It's okay.

1349
02:03:20,791 --> 02:03:21,791
You should go.

1350
02:03:26,375 --> 02:03:29,208
I promise I'll do my best
to take care of Hima.

1351
02:03:32,833 --> 02:03:35,750
So he'll live as long as possible.

1352
02:05:04,125 --> 02:05:05,166
What are you reading?

1353
02:05:05,250 --> 02:05:06,666
I'm counting snowflakes.

1354
02:05:08,583 --> 02:05:10,750
It says,

1355
02:05:10,833 --> 02:05:14,708
"The Old Dog promised the girl,

1356
02:05:15,375 --> 02:05:17,916
'Until snow falls in Thailand,

1357
02:05:18,000 --> 02:05:20,291
I will never leave you.'"

1358
02:05:22,208 --> 02:05:25,125
{\an8}My mom says it never snows in Thailand.

1359
02:05:25,208 --> 02:05:28,458
Does it mean that this dog is immortal?

1360
02:05:38,958 --> 02:05:39,875
Hima!

1361
02:05:50,708 --> 02:05:51,791
Come here.

1362
02:06:07,041 --> 02:06:09,708
You look way cooler in real life.

1363
02:06:24,208 --> 02:06:25,750
Let's make it through this year, okay?

1364
02:07:03,583 --> 02:07:05,500
You're one tough dog. You know that?

1365
02:07:13,291 --> 02:07:14,416
Tired?

1366
02:07:22,666 --> 02:07:24,875
Close your eyes for ten minutes.

1367
02:07:33,000 --> 02:07:34,458
But if that's not enough…

1368
02:07:40,375 --> 02:07:41,958
you can just fall right asleep.

1369
02:08:48,833 --> 02:08:50,666
Where are you taking me, Hima?

1370
02:09:15,041 --> 02:09:16,666
Gohan!

1371
02:09:18,375 --> 02:09:20,583
Thank you!

1372
02:09:24,458 --> 02:09:26,500
You're all grown up.

1373
02:09:27,166 --> 02:09:30,083
You won't fit in this box anymore.

1374
02:09:44,166 --> 02:09:45,166
Brownie.

1375
